{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions","id":1537817,"title":"[M20] Correspondence Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-06-28T06:38:22-07:00","id":1537817,"title":"[M20] Correspondence Questions","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> I am confused with the write up in the M20 core and on the HYDT book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Correspondence Core P.513</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">On its own, Correspondence allows the mage to reach<br /> across distances, even to places she cannot see or touch.<b> At<br /> Rank 2 or higher, she can grasp items and work with them<br /> from a distance. To manipulate other objects or beings in ways<br /> other than physical contact, however, that mage must combine<br /> Correspondence with another Sphere \u2013 typically a Pattern<br /> Sphere (Forces, Life, or Matter)</b><br /> ...<br /> <b>Despite its ability to warp space and distance,<br /> Correspondence deals only with whole Patterns</b>, unless a target<br /> has been altered by another Pattern Sphere; Correspondence<br /> alone, for example, cannot teleport someone\u2019s head off \u2013 the<br /> mage would need to use Life magick to separate the head from<br /> its body. <b>A gun, on the other hand, could be snatched away by<br /> Correspondence alone</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Imagine a mage at 1 km away from a soldier that is fully armed (loaded rifle, loaded pistol, some grenades on him). The mage has a telescope, so clear line of sight and the mage wants to:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Using Correspondence ALONE, remove the pin of a grenade the soldier is carrying. Is this possible? If so, what level of Correspondence is needed? The pin is a singular whole pattern.</li> <li>Using Correspondence ALONE, take a grenade the soldier is carrying. Is this possible? If so, what level of Correspondence is needed? Is the grenade a singular whole pattern for this purpose?</li> <li>Using Correspondence ALONE, remove a singular bullet the pistol or the rifle has inside. Is this possible? If so, what level of Correspondence is needed? The bullet is a singular whole pattern.</li> <li>Using Correspondence ALONE, remove the pistol/rifle. Is this possible? If so, what level of Correspondence is needed? Is the weapon a singular whole pattern for this purpose?</li> </ol>Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-28T12:47:54-07:00","id":1537836,"title":"","content":"All of these are questions having to do with what \u201ca single, whole Pattern\u201d is. And it's <i>not </i>clear that pins and bullets qualify; not when inserted into a grenade or gun, respectively: a case could be made that a bullet is an integral part of \u201ca loaded gun\u201d, and removing the bullet would transform it into \u201can unloaded gun\u201d. Likewise, pulling the pin from a grenade transforms it from \u201can inert grenade\u201d to \u201ca live grenade\u201d. <br /> <br /> By removing the bullet or pin, you're altering the mechanism; and the mechanism is the Pattern. <br /> <br /> On the other hand, the soldier is an organism that's carrying several mechanisms. Assuming that Prime 1 hasn't been used to make his guns or grenades (or clothes, etc.) part of his Pattern, they're separate Patterns for the purpose of Correspondence. So yeah; you can use Correspondence to port away the gun, grenades, or clothes, barring deliberate efforts to prevent that; but if you want to port away a bullet or a pin from a gun or grenade, you need Matter as well as Correspondence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-28T16:41:00-07:00","id":1537838,"title":"","content":"This is largely a matter for the ST but I would rule the following:<br /> <br /> The pin is part of the grenade. Matter is required.<br /> <br /> The grenade and the gun can be taken. The grenade and pistol are Corr 2. Depending on size the rifle might need Corr 3.<br /> <br /> Bullets are separate patterns but there is no line of sight to them so it will require a lot more successes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-28T16:43:19-07:00","id":1537839,"title":"","content":"1. Using Correspondence ALONE, remove the pin of a grenade the soldier is carrying. Is this possible? If so, what level of Correspondence is needed? The pin is a singular whole pattern.<br /> <br /> This is not possible with Correspondence alone. The pin is a part of the grenade's pattern in the same way that a bottle of water is a single whole pattern. If you wish to pull the pin of a grenade from a distance using correspondences, you would need Matter 2 with Correspondence 2. Matter 2 because the pin of the grenade is a fairly simple matter pattern.<br /> <br /> 2. Using Correspondence ALONE, take a grenade the soldier is carrying. Is this possible? If so, what level of Correspondence is needed? Is the grenade a singular whole pattern for this purpose?<br /> <br /> The Grenade itself is indeed a singular whole pattern, but aportation, (the teleportation of living things or objects to or from the caster) requires a sphere rank equal to the complexity of the object being teleported. To teleport simple life like plants or insects is Corr 2 Life 2, More complex animals like a small cat would need Corr 3 Life 3, while big animals including Humans would need Life 4 Corr 4. Though by that point you could just open a gate and allow them to enter with Corr 4 alone<br /> <br /> As for the grenade, simple patterns, i.e. matter patterns that are relatively small and made up of only one material only need Corr 2 Matter 2 to aportate, More involved objects which are larger or have multiple aspects fo them, such as a bottle of water, require Matter 3 Corr 3, and rather complex objects such as machines require Matter 4 Corr 4.<br /> <br /> I would say that a grenade, being a bunch of scrap metal encased in plastic with explosives in there, counts as a complex objects, and so requires Corr 4 Matter 4 to aportate.<br /> <br /> 3. Using Correspondence ALONE, remove a singular bullet the pistol or the rifle has inside. Is this possible? If so, what level of Correspondence is needed? The bullet is a singular whole pattern.<br /> <br /> This is not possible with Correspondence alone for much the same reasons as mentioned above. While the bullets remain inside the gun, they are part of the gun's pattern as the intent of a gun is to fire said bullets. If you wish to aportate the bullet, I would consider this to need Corr 3 Matter 3.<br /> <br /> 4. Using Correspondence ALONE, remove the pistol/rifle. Is this possible? If so, what level of Correspondence is needed? Is the weapon a singular whole pattern for this purpose?<br /> <br /> Also not possible, not because the pistol is not a whole pattern, but because, once again, aportation requires the same level in the pattern sphere. Corr 4 Matter 4.<br /> <br /> Apportation is a Correspondence 2 level effect. But the reason Correspondence rank required changes is that you can't cast Correspondence effects at range unless you have correspondence at the same rank as the highest sphere in the effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 06-28-2024, 07:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-28T16:59:37-07:00","id":1537840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1537839#post1537839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Using Correspondence ALONE, remove the pin of a grenade the soldier is carrying. Is this possible? If so, what level of Correspondence is needed? The pin is a singular whole pattern.<br /> <br /> This is not possible with Correspondence alone. The pin is a part of the grenade's pattern in the same way that a bottle of water is a single whole pattern. If you wish to pull the pin of a grenade from a distance using correspondences, you would need Matter 2 with Correspondence 2. Matter 2 because the pin of the grenade is a fairly simple matter pattern.<br /> <br /> 2. Using Correspondence ALONE, take a grenade the soldier is carrying. Is this possible? If so, what level of Correspondence is needed? Is the grenade a singular whole pattern for this purpose?<br /> <br /> The Grenade itself is indeed a singular whole pattern, but aportation, (the teleportation of living things or objects to or from the caster) requires a sphere rank equal to the complexity of the object being teleported. To teleport simple life like plants or insects is Corr 2 Life 2, More complex animals like a small cat would need Corr 3 Life 3, while big animals including Humans would need Life 4 Corr 4. Though by that point you could just open a gate and allow them to enter with Corr 4 alone<br /> <br /> As for the grenade, simple patterns, i.e. matter patterns that are relatively small and made up of only one material only need Corr 2 Matter 2 to aportate, More involved objects which are larger or have multiple aspects fo them, such as a bottle of water, require Matter 3 Corr 3, and rather complex objects such as machines require Matter 4 Corr 4.<br /> <br /> I would say that a grenade, being a bunch of scrap metal encased in plastic with explosives in there, counts as a complex objects, and so requires Corr 4 Matter 4 to aportate.<br /> <br /> 3. Using Correspondence ALONE, remove a singular bullet the pistol or the rifle has inside. Is this possible? If so, what level of Correspondence is needed? The bullet is a singular whole pattern.<br /> <br /> This is not possible with Correspondence alone for much the same reasons as mentioned above. While the bullets remain inside the gun, they are part of the gun's pattern as the intent of a gun is to fire said bullets. If you wish to aportate the bullet, I would consider this to need Corr 3 Matter 3.<br /> <br /> 4. Using Correspondence ALONE, remove the pistol/rifle. Is this possible? If so, what level of Correspondence is needed? Is the weapon a singular whole pattern for this purpose?<br /> <br /> Also not possible, not because the pistol is not a whole pattern, but because, once again, aportation requires the same level in the pattern sphere. Corr 4 Matter 4.<br /> <br /> Apportation is a Correspondence 2 level effect. But the reason Correspondence rank required changes is that you can't cast Correspondence effects at range unless you have correspondence at the same rank as the highest sphere in the effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>The examples in M20 get this wrong a lot but Correspondence explicitly does not need another sphere to move a whole pattern.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-29T04:01:07-07:00","id":1537854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1537840#post1537840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The examples in M20 get this wrong a lot but Correspondence explicitly does not need another sphere to move a whole pattern.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quote from Mage core 2e Pg 189<br /> <br /> Apportation - By pressing against the fabric of space, a mage may create a pinprick in the Tapestry. While too small to step through, such rifts allow the mage to grasp a distant item and pull it through - or send it away - <b>using Life or Matter</b>. This only works on very small, simple objects. A third rank variation allows the mystick to forge a connection to some simple objects - <b>again with Life or Matter </b>- which allows it to levitate or fly for the Effect's duration.<br /> <br /> Quote from Mage core Revised Pg 159<br /> <br /> Apportation - Although the rudiments of Correspondence are insufficient to actually teleport safely over long distances, a mage can affect some small Patterns. A quick Effect causes an object or creature to transport to or from the mage. <b>The mage must use the appropriate Pattern Sphere, typically Life or Matter</b>. Apportation can't affect any Pattern more complex than the mage's Correspondence knowledge. That is, even a Master of Life or Matter can transport only very simple Patterns with this limited understanding of Correspondence (plants and very simple animals for life, basic homogenous substances for Matter)<br /> <br /> Quote from M20 Pg 513<br /> <br /> By adding <b>Life or Matter</b> to Rank 2 Correspondence, the mage can grasp small items or organisms (housecat-sized or smaller) and then pull them through tiny holes in space. This lets her snatch business cards, guns, rabbits, and such from another location, apparently pulling them out of nowhere.<br /> ...<br /> Also, by combining Correspondence 3 with <b>Forces, Life, or Matter, </b>the mage can move things around from a distance, levitating, manipulating, or teleporting them without physical contact.<br /> <br /> <br /> This facet of Correspondence has been in there for ages and has been consistent across all editions. You cannot teleport objects or living things to or away from you unless you have the appropriate pattern sphere.<br /> <br /> Correspondence alone can allow you to:<br /> <br /> at Corr 2 extend your senses so you can see, feel, hear, or otherwise objects or people without directly affecting them.<br /> at Corr 3 you can pierce space to teleport yourself and a number of things you can carry with you. You can't bring big bulky stuff, but you can bring other people with you if they are a part of your life pattern (such as if they have been consecrated either by you or you to them using Prime 2 Life 3, or if your ST rules that you can extend your targets to include others along with you, however that is an interpretation rather than a RAW reading.<br /> at Corr 4 you can rip holes in space that allow for multiple things to enter and exit. You can also co-locate yourself, and one of your several versions may happily pick up an object, but if you want that object to snap back with you when you stop co-locating, you'll need use of Matter within this spell","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 06-29-2024, 07:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-29T04:38:01-07:00","id":1537855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1537854#post1537854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Quote from Mage core 2e Pg 189<br /> <br /> Apportation - By pressing against the fabric of space, a mage may create a pinprick in the Tapestry. While too small to step through, such rifts allow the mage to grasp a distant item and pull it through - or send it away - <b>using Life or Matter</b>. This only works on very small, simple objects. A third rank variation allows the mystick to forge a connection to some simple objects - <b>again with Life or Matter </b>- which allows it to levitate or fly for the Effect's duration.<br /> <br /> Quote from Mage core Revised Pg 159<br /> <br /> Apportation - Although the rudiments of Correspondence are insufficient to actually teleport safely over long distances, a mage can affect some small Patterns. A quick Effect causes an object or creature to transport to or from the mage. <b>The mage must use the appropriate Pattern Sphere, typically Life or Matter</b>. Apportation can't affect any Pattern more complex than the mage's Correspondence knowledge. That is, even a Master of Life or Matter can transport only very simple Patterns with this limited understanding of Correspondence (plants and very simple animals for life, basic homogenous substances for Matter)<br /> <br /> Quote from M20 Pg 513<br /> <br /> By adding <b>Life or Matter</b> to Rank 2 Correspondence, the mage can grasp small items or organisms (housecat-sized or smaller) and then pull them through tiny holes in space. This lets her snatch business cards, guns, rabbits, and such from another location, apparently pulling them out of nowhere.<br /> ...<br /> Also, by combining Correspondence 3 with <b>Forces, Life, or Matter, </b>the mage can move things around from a distance, levitating, manipulating, or teleporting them without physical contact.<br /> <br /> <br /> This facet of Correspondence has been in there for ages and has been consistent across all editions. You cannot teleport objects or living things to or away from you unless you have the appropriate pattern sphere.<br /> <br /> Correspondence alone can allow you to:<br /> <br /> at Corr 2 extend your senses so you can see, feel, hear, or otherwise objects or people without directly affecting them.<br /> at Corr 3 you can pierce space to teleport yourself and a number of things you can carry with you. You can't bring big bulky stuff, but you can bring other people with you if they are a part of your life pattern (such as if they have been consecrated either by you or you to them using Prime 2 Life 3, or if your ST rules that you can extend your targets to include others along with you, however that is an interpretation rather than a RAW reading.<br /> at Corr 4 you can rip holes in space that allow for multiple things to enter and exit. You can also co-locate yourself, and one of your several versions may happily pick up an object, but if you want that object to snap back with you when you stop co-locating, you'll need use of Matter within this spell</div> </div> </div> </div>Understoond and found the references, but then... The whole book is inconsistent! What about the &quot;<b>A gun, on the other hand, could be snatched away by Correspondence alone</b>.&quot; this is not true at all then.<br /> <br /> It is so frustrating that the spheres effects are not consistently defined even in the same book. Bad writting all around?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-29T04:44:46-07:00","id":1537856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1537855#post1537855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Understoond and found the references, but then... The whole book is inconsistent! What about the &quot;<b>A gun, on the other hand, could be snatched away by Correspondence alone</b>.&quot; this is not true at all then.<br /> <br /> It is so frustrating that the spheres effects are not consistently defined even in the same book. Bad writting all around?</div> </div> </div> </div>This would be in the case of using Correspondence 4 to make portals or carry bulky items or many people with you while you teleport. You can't, fore example, have the gun enter but leave behind the bullets, or allow a person to enter but severe their legs by closing the portal on them. Correspondence alone is sufficient for the gun as a whole object to come with you in the portal though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-29T09:24:35-07:00","id":1537861,"title":"","content":"I have numerous threads dealing with inconsistencies in M20. It\u2019s most likely the result of inconsistent and incomplete revisions. Even the individual ranks of spheres have meaningless sentences and contradictory rules. <br /> <br /> In the end, the base section of Correspondence lists a very clear ruling and lists the logic behind it and that has enormous weight. <br /> <br /> The sections requiring pattern spheres for teleportation do not give a justification. They do not give clear guidance on what the pattern spheres are even doing (altering, transmuting, etc.) which is rather important for figuring out what rank they are supposed to be. <br /> <br /> Between those alternatives I have to give credence to the former. It\u2019s not even a hard choice.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-29T10:28:30-07:00","id":1537862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1537861#post1537861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have numerous threads dealing with inconsistencies in M20. It\u2019s most likely the result of inconsistent and incomplete revisions. Even the individual ranks of spheres have meaningless sentences and contradictory rules.<br /> <br /> In the end, the base section of Correspondence lists a very clear ruling and lists the logic behind it and that has enormous weight.<br /> <br /> The sections requiring pattern spheres for teleportation do not give a justification. They do not give clear guidance on what the pattern spheres are even doing (altering, transmuting, etc.) which is rather important for figuring out what rank they are supposed to be.<br /> <br /> Between those alternatives I have to give credence to the former. It\u2019s not even a hard choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say the fact that this rule is consistent between several editions gives it far more weight.<br /> As for what the pattern spheres are doing, the simple answer is transmutation, in specific you are transmuting their spatial relationship. This is why Corr 2 Matter 2 only allows you to apportate simple matter patterns of a homogenous matter type, as this is the level of transmutation that Matter 2 is limited to. Matter 3 transmutation enables more complex objects with multiple parts to them, while Matter 4 is required for machines and complex alloys, especially ones that contain elements of non Matter spheres such as Wonders.<br /> <br /> Similarly, Life 2 is required for simple life, and Life 4 for complex life, the same levels required for transmutation of a life pattern ( Though you could argue Life 3 as this is the level of Life pattern transmutation required to heal or harm others)<br /> <br /> This is the usual way that the pattern spheres are used with other spheres for the purposes of evoking change, you need the rank at which transmutation is possible. And to reiterate, the change in this case is their connection with their spatial location.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-29T10:43:03-07:00","id":1537863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1537862#post1537862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would say the fact that this rule is consistent between several editions gives it far more weight.<br /> As for what the pattern spheres are doing, the simple answer is transmutation, in specific you are transmuting their spatial relationship. This is why Corr 2 Matter 2 only allows you to apportate simple matter patterns of a homogenous matter type, as this is the level of transmutation that Matter 2 is limited to. Matter 3 transmutation enables more complex objects with multiple parts to them, while Matter 4 is required for machines and complex alloys, especially ones that contain elements of non Matter spheres such as Wonders.<br /> <br /> Similarly, Life 2 is required for simple life, and Life 4 for complex life, the same levels required for transmutation of a life pattern ( Though you could argue Life 3 as this is the level of Life pattern transmutation required to heal or harm others)<br /> <br /> This is the usual way that the pattern spheres are used with other spheres for the purposes of evoking change, you need the rank at which transmutation is possible. And to reiterate, the change in this case is their connection with their spatial location.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If transmutation included location you could teleport things over sensory distances without correspondence at all. There\u2019s no indication that\u2019s possible. I can\u2019t get behind that as a explanation.<br /> <br /> Also, Life 2 is the alteration level not the transmutation level.<br /> <br /> One way or another we have to disregard some of these quotes. If you go with a different interpretation than I do, that\u2019s fine. As far as I\u2019m concerned, though, it\u2019s clear Correspondence doesn\u2019t need help and that\u2019s the way I\u2019m advising people.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-29T11:17:07-07:00","id":1537866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1537863#post1537863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If transmutation included location you could teleport things over sensory distances without correspondence at all. There\u2019s no indication that\u2019s possible. I can\u2019t get behind that as a explanation.<br /> <br /> Also, Life 2 is the alteration level not the transmutation level.<br /> <br /> One way or another we have to disregard some of these quotes. If you go with a different interpretation than I do, that\u2019s fine. As far as I\u2019m concerned, though, it\u2019s clear Correspondence doesn\u2019t need help and that\u2019s the way I\u2019m advising people.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Life 2 allows transmutation of plants... That is how you get blossoms to bloom or trees to grow. But if you want to limit it to Life 3, then by all means, you do you.<br /> <br /> And the idea that you don't need correspondence to teleport things over a sensory distance is a misunderstanding of what is happening here.<br /> <br /> Remember, correspondence is not the sphere of space, locations, or even of sensory distances. It is the sphere of connections. All things are connected together intrinsically, but the strength of those connections varies, which creates the perception of distance. What Correspondence taps in to is manipulating the strength of these connections. With apportation what you are doing is changing the strength of connection between the object and its current environment such that it's connection to the table becomes far weaker than its connection to your hand. This is a property which is contained within the pattern itself, as is the case with all patterns.<br /> <br /> The complexity of the object is taking in to account that the matter pattern itself has its own connections, ones which Matter itself do indeed deal with. Matter 3 allows you to disperse a matter pattern in to a gas, essentially forcing all those connections to cease and the object to be repelled, similarly Matter 3 also allows the fusion of objects, forging stronger connections. Matter 4 takes this step further by allowing fusions to complete that new alloys are created.<br /> <br /> Those connections are very much under the purview of Matter and Matter alone. But it's metaphysical connections, the ones that are imperceivable without use of the correspondence sphere itself, that is what Correspondence is required to change, but in order to fix those qualities to the matter pattern itself, both spheres are required, for Correspondence alone is not an external, it can only affect your own connections, either via your senses or your familiarities. But it is entirely from your perspective.<br /> <br /> This is the same reason why you need the pattern spheres if you wish to lock in effects to make trinkets, you are transmuting them in such a way as to hold the change in the environment at a metaphysical level.<br /> <br /> Now, with Correspondence 3 alone you can alter the strength of relationships between objects which are right infront of you, this is called chaining. And what this does it change how close they are to one another for the purposes of the correspondence chart, but if you want to make something at the range of Body Sample, then that requires the pattern in question to be transmuted so fundamentally that is registers as a part of yourself on a metaphysical level.<br /> <br /> You don't necessarily need Correspondence to do this, it can be done by investing personal quintessence in to the object with Prime 1 or by puting a piece of your soul in to the object with Spirit 5, though the spirit 5 method would most certainly need Matter in order to have your soul be transmused with the object itself (otherwise you could just awaken the spirit of the object and transmute the spirit to contain an aspect of your soul, but that can go so wrong in so many ways).<br /> Prime 1 transmutation is generally easier, and because it is dealing with solidified quintessence in the object itself, no transmutation is actually taking place. But if you wish to consecrate a Life pattern with Prime 2, then you do need the relevant transmutation Life sphere because Life pattern quintessence is not static, it is constantly ebbing and flowing, so in order to the maintain the concecration to any degree of usability, locking it in with Life is required.<br /> <br /> That is how the pattern spheres function, metaphysically all aspects of the spheres are flowing through them, all objects, living beings, and energies will have a Resonance on them (mind), a spiritual entite about them (Spirit), a place within the grander scheme of fate (Entropy), A level of quintessence allowing them to subsist in reality (Prime), a constant relationship with the (usually) forward march of time (Time) and a whole rolladex of connections to other objects, people, places, locations, memories, etc (Correspondence).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-30T10:28:37-07:00","id":1537897,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ll go into more depth when I\u2019m back at a computer, but my short response is that all of that is a reasonable paradigm for a Mage to hold in game, but it doesn\u2019t work well as a universal explanation of game mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-30T12:41:05-07:00","id":1537900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1537897#post1537897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ll go into more depth when I\u2019m back at a computer, but my short response is that all of that is a reasonable paradigm for a Mage to hold in game, but it doesn\u2019t work well as a universal explanation of game mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>the idea or Correspondence as the sphere of connections is in the text for pretty much all editions, it stands above paradigm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-01T08:17:34-07:00","id":1537948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1537866#post1537866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Life 2 allows transmutation of plants... That is how you get blossoms to bloom or trees to grow. But if you want to limit it to Life 3, then by all means, you do you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that I'm advocating against using Life at all for this, &quot;you do you&quot; is a rather odd response.<br /> <br /> In any case, my point in bringing up the Life 2/Life 3 distinction is that your advice is less helpful for other people than you think it is. You are clearly referring to small changes, which Mage 20th usually refers to as Alteration, but you are using the term Transmutation which is a much greater and more fundamental change. Indeed, the Life 2 writeup on page 516 explicitly says it is not capable of transmutation. Someone following your advice is going to use Life 3, not Life 2, because it looks like that's what you are advising.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1537900#post1537900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> the idea or Correspondence as the sphere of connections is in the text for pretty much all editions, it stands above paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, but what you expressed went well beyond that simple idea. Instead, you have a complicated explanation for how it works that is neither obvious or intuitive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1537866#post1537866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...All things are connected together intrinsically, but the strength of those connections varies, which creates the perception of distance...<br /> <br /> ...With apportation what you are doing is changing the strength of connection between the object and its current environment such that it's connection to the table becomes far weaker than its connection to your hand...<br /> <br /> ...This is a property which is contained within the pattern itself, as is the case with all patterns...<br /> <br /> ...in order to fix those qualities to the matter pattern itself, both spheres are required, for Correspondence alone is not an external, it can only affect your own connections...<br /> <br /> etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is where you really start getting into something that is more in game paradigm than functional game system. You've started adding things like <i>Distance Is the Illusion or Byproduct of Connection</i> and that <i>Connections are Intrinsic to the Pattern Itself</i>. Those principles are effective in game character beliefs, but they are not at all obvious in the Correspondence writeup itself. Indeed, distance as illusion is explicitly referred to as an in-game approach to Correspondence.<br /> <br /> And again, we are dealing with a rules contradiction here. If it takes that much explanation to justify going one way, I'm not going that way. If it is that unclear how to adjudicate things if we go that way, I'm not going that way.<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-01T15:40:40-07:00","id":1537963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1537948#post1537948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that I'm advocating against using Life at all for this, &quot;you do you&quot; is a rather odd response.</div> </div> </div> </div>[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> I'm just telling you what the books are saying and providing a reason that I believe fits the metaphysics as established. If you wish to disregard it to use fewer spheres, or use the explanation to justify making the effect require higher ranks, then 'you do you' seems entirely appropriate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1537948#post1537948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In any case, my point in bringing up the Life 2/Life 3 distinction is that your advice is less helpful for other people than you think it is. You are clearly referring to small changes, which Mage 20th usually refers to as Alteration, but you are using the term Transmutation which is a much greater and more fundamental change. Indeed, the Life 2 writeup on page 516 explicitly says it is not capable of transmutation. Someone following your advice is going to use Life 3, not Life 2, because it looks like that's what you are advising.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Seems to me like you understand what I'm trying to say, and that's all I really want. Whether or not you personally wish to use the explanation or not is not really my concern, the fact that you are engaging with the idea to consider how it could be better communicated is enough for me to know you get it.<br /> <br /> Though I will point out that Life 2 can transmute, it just can't transmute &quot;in to other states of being&quot; like a fish in to a tree. This is not unlike how Matter 2 cannot transmute in to other states. Unless we wish to decree that changing your hair color and skin color doesn't count as transmutation for some reason. But I digress, this is clearly a point of word choice than it a difference in conceptual understanding.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1537948#post1537948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed, but what you expressed went well beyond that simple idea. Instead, you have a complicated explanation for how it works that is neither obvious or intuitive<br /> <br /> This is where you really start getting into something that is more in game paradigm than functional game system. You've started adding things like <i>Distance Is the Illusion or Byproduct of Connection</i> and that <i>Connections are Intrinsic to the Pattern Itself</i>. Those principles are effective in game character beliefs, but they are not at all obvious in the Correspondence writeup itself. Indeed, distance as illusion is explicitly referred to as an in-game approach to Correspondence.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>While the concept of the illusion is fairly paradigmactic, I'll grant you that, the idea that connections aren't a part of a pattern is incorrect. Every mage book that speaks about correspondence, and that includes the core books, the tradition books, and even the technocratic books, talk about connections between objects, people, places, etc, as the thing that this sphere is operating on. This is the reason why things which are more familiar to you are easier to engage with using correspondence than things you have nothing to do with. The connection is stronger. Every object in the world has such connections, be it a book with their authors or their readers, a watch with its makers or its owners, if it can possibly appear as anything on the correspondence chart beyond no connection, it has those connections inherently within it. That is why the correspondence chart works the way it does, and it's why you can use correspondence 1 to not only sense these connections, but the strength of these connections too.<br /> <br /> You could argue that correspondence can be used to forge connections between objects, but in the same way that Resonance is an inherent part of a location once it is established, so are connections, and like resonance they come about from completely mundane interactions. I make the parallels with Fate, Spirit, and Mind to illustrate by, just how every object as a spirit that can be awakened with Spirit 3, a relationship with fate which can be tuned with Entropy 3 (whether you believe it to be how close to chaos it is, or how a part of destiny it is), and a resonance emanating from it which can be tuned with Mind 2 (or Prime), said objects also have connections. And when it comes to their environment, the strongest connections they have are the ones with the areas they are currently within, one of the reasons why line of sight is always the strongest connection, next to body sample.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1537948#post1537948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> <br /> And again, we are dealing with a rules contradiction here. If it takes that much explanation to justify going one way, I'm not going that way. If it is that unclear how to adjudicate things if we go that way, I'm not going that way.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I gave you a simple explanation, you didn't like it and seemed to think it was spurious. So I gave you my thoughts on it since I thought that would be of interest to you rather than dismissed as wasted effort. It is a little upsetting, but if you have decided I am wrong, then I must be wrong.<br /> <br /> Though for clarity, The simple explanation will be reiterated here:<br /> It has required Matter and Life for those effects in 2e, Revised, and in M20, this ruling being so consistent across multiple editions is pretty indicative that it has intended to work like this for a while.<br /> Metaphysically, it is because you are severing its connection with where it was, and restoring its connection to where you are, that can be seen as a form of transmutation (or alteration if you prefer that word for Life patterns).<br /> Game design wise, the reason that it requires more spheres is because without said investment, Correspondence on its own becomes a bit...silly. Just 2 points in correspondence to teleport pretty much whatever you want wherever you like. An Arete 2 mage could pretty easily teleport an atomic bomb to whatever location they desire, rather than such a feat require Matter 5 Corr 5, (the level of matter required to transmute radioactive material without Forces) and thus be locked away until one becomes a master, at which point such a mage would have to be pretty dedicated to desire such a gambit. Similarly one could make the argument that you can start teleporting people &quot;if they are small enough&quot; with Corr 2. And when you can start teleporting people to and from yourself without any involvement of you in the process... no other sphere really need apply. So from a design perspective I would ask you to reconsider it as a house rule if you want any form of gravitas in your games to be maintained. But hey, some people like their mages gonzo, and who am I to tell you not to. I just can't personally recommend them.<br /> <br /> But in answer to the questions as being asked, this is how correspondence is written to work. I have addressed what is seen as a contradiction and explained my reasoning for why I believe this is the intended ruling out of the possible other interpretations. If you wish to ask clarification I am happy to further elaborate, otherwise by all means express your own reasoning for preferring your ruling. There is no reason either of us need convince the other of anything. The discussion is open for all to read and conclude as they best judge.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 07-02-2024, 05:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-02T12:01:06-07:00","id":1538008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1537963#post1537963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just telling you what the books are saying and providing a reason that I believe fits the metaphysics as established. If you wish to disregard it to use fewer spheres, or use the explanation to justify making the effect require higher ranks, then 'you do you' seems entirely appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because M20 outright contradicts itself on this point, we both have to disregard part of it. The discussion is about which part of it we disregard and why. Everyone has to do themselves, because they certainly can't do M20 as written.<br /> <br /> Possibly there was a better way of saying that than &quot;Everyone has to do themselves...&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1537963#post1537963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I gave you a simple explanation, you didn't like it and seemed to think it was spurious. So I gave you my thoughts on it since I thought that would be of interest to you rather than dismissed as wasted effort. It is a little upsetting, but if you have decided I am wrong, then I must be wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not spurious. It just assumes a metaphysics that is not necessary and it is open to more problems in understanding than I want to deal with when resolving a rules contradiction. Of course I'm interested in your approach, but that doesn't mean I'm going to agree with it.<br /> <br /> I'd love to have grand high arbiter power and judge you wrong or right, but you are giving me too much credit. I've repeatedly said its fine if you go with a different interpretation than I do.<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-02T12:15:05-07:00","id":1538009,"title":"","content":"The way I see it, Correspondence Alone is very clearly stated in exactly the position in the book a Correspondence rule should be. It has a consistent logic behind it, it tracks with the stated powers of Correspondence and the general approach to calculating requirements. The contradicting statements are harder to find and lack explanation.<br /> <br /> Now M20 is a bit of a mess. This is hardly the only time contradictions and ambiguities arise. Like I said earlier, I think the magic rules were overhauled at least once during writing and a lot of artifacts of the older rules were missed in editing. Over time I've developed a few guidelines for working through the mess. There are three relevant ones here:<br /> <br /> 1) Spheres should be able to accomplish their primary abilities without help. When Entropy 4 is given as the level for Altering Life, it can Alter Life. It doesn't need help from the Life sphere. Any exceptions should be clear and easy to understand.<br /> <br /> 2) Mages don't need Pattern Spheres to target. That is, a mage can cast a Forces based pushing spell on objects without using Matter and on creatures without using Life. The same is true for most if not all effects. Locking Spheres are a thing, but Targeting Spheres are not.<br /> <br /> 3) When dealing with ambiguities, give more weight to the lowest reasonable sphere requirements.<br /> <br /> For all of these reasons, I use the whole pattern rules on Page 513 and I sideline or ignore contrary statements elsewhere.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-11T21:13:48-07:00","id":1538460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions#post1537817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greetings,<br /> <br /> I am confused with the write up in the M20 core and on the HYDT book.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Imagine a mage at 1 km away from a soldier that is fully armed (loaded rifle, loaded pistol, some grenades on him). The mage has a telescope, so clear line of sight and the mage wants to:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Using Correspondence ALONE, remove the pin of a grenade the soldier is carrying. Is this possible? If so, what level of Correspondence is needed? The pin is a singular whole pattern.</li> <li>Using Correspondence ALONE, take a grenade the soldier is carrying. Is this possible? If so, what level of Correspondence is needed? Is the grenade a singular whole pattern for this purpose?</li> <li>Using Correspondence ALONE, remove a singular bullet the pistol or the rifle has inside. Is this possible? If so, what level of Correspondence is needed? The bullet is a singular whole pattern.</li> <li>Using Correspondence ALONE, remove the pistol/rifle. Is this possible? If so, what level of Correspondence is needed? Is the weapon a singular whole pattern for this purpose?</li> </ol>Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>1 - Correspondence 2, Matter 2. If you're seeing the pin with a telescope, this is considered &quot;line of sight&quot; for the table of reach and difficulty.<br /> Edit: sorry, you asked for Corr alone. That would be Corr 4, just as all bellow.<br /> 2 - RAW you'd need Correspondence 4, but both this requirement and the requirement above are completely idiotic, and in my opinion, Correspondence is just simply awfully written, like so, so much stuff is in Mage.<br /> 3 - Corr 4 again, and again all the same considerations as above.<br /> 4 - Same as above.<br /> <br /> Correspondence is one of the most horribly written Spheres out there (but not the only one by a long shot, and not even the worse - that would be Forces. Oh boy, don't even let me start on Forces!)<br /> <br /> Correspondence don't even begin to make sense in the sort of &quot;backbone&quot; structure of how Spheres are supposed to behave, which is 1 - Sensorial Magic, 2 - Manipulation, 3 - Control, 4 - Transmutation, 5 - Mastery.<br /> <br /> What would make much more sense would be:<br /> 1 - Sense Space<br /> You can perceive everything all around you, including in your back, above and even bellow you.<br /> If you want to understand what this means, just think about Batman's &quot;Sonar Vision&quot; in the Dark Knight movie. So basically, you can &quot;see&quot; behind walls and behind obstacles. But more than just that, you also get a 360 degrees vision.<br /> <br /> You also get an absolute sense of location, meaning that you can never get lost. You may not know where you're at if, for example, someone throws you in a jungle, but if you decide to go in a direction, you'll never walk in circles.<br /> <br /> You can also precisely determine any sort of distance measurements. Even in an unknown jungle, you'll know how many miles away from your home (a well know point of reference; it could be any other too) you are, and in what direction it is.<br /> <br /> You could also use a picture from the Eiffel tower as a reference point, even if you never visited Paris; it would just be harder (just check the table for successes). Or, you could &quot;track&quot; someone having a personal object from the target (a body sample, like a hair, would make such an effect to be almost trivial)<br /> <br /> 2 - Far senses<br /> This is the cliche crystal ball. You can sense things far away. This also including hearing and even smell. Not much to add.<br /> <br /> 3 - Teleport<br /> Self explanatory. Teleport yourself somewhere else, or teleport something or someone somewhere else, or teleport something or someone to you.<br /> <br /> 4 - Manipulate Space.<br /> Open doorways between two places (aka portals). Amplify or shrink the Space between two points. Make a pattern occupy two (or more) different spaces at the same time.<br /> Amplifying space allows you to create the famous &quot;bags of infinity&quot; for example.<br /> <br /> 5 - Co-location<br /> Make Patterns occupy the same space at the same time. (This is SUPER powerful)<br /> <br /> So no, Aport not only is stupid for requiring other Spheres to something that is spacial manipulation only, but it is also stupid for being a lvl 2 effect, so it should never exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-11T22:20:12-07:00","id":1538463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1537866#post1537866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Life 2 allows transmutation of plants... That is how you get blossoms to bloom or trees to grow. But if you want to limit it to Life 3, then by all means, you do you.</div> </div> </div> </div>What does this has to do with anything? Nobody mentioned anything about changing something that MAKES SENSE, but we are pointing towards the fact that Correspondence obviously DOESN'T MAKE SENSE AT ALL.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the idea that you don't need correspondence to teleport things over a sensory distance is a misunderstanding of what is happening here. </div> </div> </div>No, it is not. That's exactly what it means, if we need Matter or Life to apport stuff, why do we need Corr? It makes zero sense at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Remember, correspondence is not the sphere of space, locations, or even of sensory distances. It is the sphere of connections. All things are connected together intrinsically, but the strength of those connections varies, which creates the perception of distance. What Correspondence taps in to is manipulating the strength of these connections. With apportation what you are doing is changing the strength of connection between the object and its current environment such that it's connection to the table becomes far weaker than its connection to your hand. This is a property which is contained within the pattern itself, as is the case with all patterns. </div> </div> </div>Cool story bro. I'm sure that this esoteric-babbling is what you claim to be the &quot;reality&quot; at your little hermetic club.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, between me and my boys in black, we are pretty sure that Correspondence is the Sphere of Space. That's what &quot;da sCience&quot; says. Even those VA traitors agree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The complexity of the object is taking in to account that the matter pattern itself has its own connections, ones which Matter itself do indeed deal with. Matter 3 allows you to disperse a matter pattern in to a gas, essentially forcing all those connections to cease and the object to be repelled, similarly Matter 3 also allows the fusion of objects, forging stronger connections. Matter 4 takes this step further by allowing fusions to complete that new alloys are created. </div> </div> </div>More mystic-babble that has nothing to do with the point. We're not talking about Matter; we all know what Matter does, and by the way, nowhere is it given that Matter allows matter to be teleported from point A to point B, and we are talking about Correspondence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Those connections are very much under the purview of Matter and Matter alone. But it's metaphysical connections, the ones that are imperceivable without use of the correspondence sphere itself, that is what Correspondence is required to change, but in order to fix those qualities to the matter pattern itself, both spheres are required, for Correspondence alone is not an external, it can only affect your own connections, either via your senses or your familiarities. But it is entirely from your perspective. </div> </div> </div>That was entirely non-sequitur. &quot;Correspondence only affect your own connections&quot;. WHAT??? What the hell am I reading here?<br /> <br /> Also, even if that was remotely true (spoilers: it ain't), how would that even begin to justify anything?<br /> <br /> So, first: here you're saying that Correspondence is a special unicorn: all other 8 Spheres (and variations) are perfectly capable of affecting anything external to the Mage himself, thank you very much, but Correspondence isn't? Lol what? Doesn't make any sense.<br /> <br /> Also: Correspondence 4 allows a Mage to create a &quot;direct connection&quot; (using your definition, which I think is too much paradigm related by the way) between 2 different spaces. There's no matter or life involved, just a &quot;connection&quot; between point A and point B. So, are you saying that Correspondence 4 allows one to make a &quot;connection between connections&quot;? Ok, the book on the table is on the table because it shares a bigger connection with the table than with my hand, and that's why I need Matter to change that (because of reasons), but if I want to create a portal between point A and B, I don't need anything else other than Correspondence...<br /> <br /> So, here's the problem, Correspondence 4 makes all that you said to become false, because Correspondence 4 shows that Correspondence is perfectly capable of manipulating the &quot;connections&quot; without needing any other Spheres.<br /> <br /> Besides, why would you need any other Spheres to begin with? Isn't Correspondence the Sphere of &quot;connections&quot; as you just said? So why don't Correspondence do what it was supposed to do by itself without needing others? Don't you think that, in this case Correspondence should be written as:<br /> <br /> Correspondence 3: you can change the &quot;connection&quot; that the book on the table has with the table, weakening that connection with the table, while strengthening it with your hand, thus transferring the book from the table to your hand.<br /> <br /> There, done. Correspondence 3, it just changed the &quot;connection&quot; between the book, the table and your hand. Why does it have to have additional Spheres randomly in it?<br /> <br /> Demanding additional Spheres is like demanding Matter to be used when you use Entropy 3, demanding Life when you use Entropy 4 or demanding Mind when you use Entropy 5.<br /> <br /> Or even worse, demanding Prime when you use &quot;Chi healing&quot; or demanding Spirit when you use &quot;Spiritual healing&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is the same reason why you need the pattern spheres if you wish to lock in effects to make trinkets, you are transmuting them in such a way as to hold the change in the environment at a metaphysical level. </div> </div> </div>If you're referring to making Talismans and such using Prime, that is absolutely NOT the reason as to why you use Pattern Spheres. Not even in a long shot.<br /> <br /> Besides, you DON'T need to use Pattern Spheres to make magic items, IF you have some to &quot;mold&quot; your Tass into the desired magic item. Granted, if you're trying to use crystals Tass to forge a sword, you'll obviously need matter because there's no mundane way to turn crystals into swords, but if you want to turn a crystal imbued with Quint into a periapt, you just need the crystal itself to do it (assuming it has enough quint into it). If you have Tass in the form of apples for instance, you DON'T need Life together with Prime to turn them into a healing potion, you can just make a juice with them.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, with Correspondence 3 alone you can alter the strength of relationships between objects which are right infront of you, this is called chaining. And what this does it change how close they are to one another for the purposes of the correspondence chart, but if you want to make something at the range of Body Sample, then that requires the pattern in question to be transmuted so fundamentally that is registers as a part of yourself on a metaphysical level. </div> </div> </div>Again, what does this have to do with anything?<br /> <br /> Also, this can also be done with Prime 1 or 2 (matter/life patterns respectively).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You don't necessarily need Correspondence to do this, it can be done by investing personal quintessence in to the object with Prime 1 or by puting a piece of your soul in to the object with Spirit 5, though the spirit 5 method would most certainly need Matter in order to have your soul be transmused with the object itself (otherwise you could just awaken the spirit of the object and transmute the spirit to contain an aspect of your soul, but that can go so wrong in so many ways). </div> </div> </div>Ah, ok. You explain the Prime stuff. Just one small correction, you don't need to invest Quint for it, you just &quot;align&quot; the resonance of the two Patterns that you're trying to bind together.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Prime 1 transmutation is generally easier, and because it is dealing with solidified quintessence in the object itself, no transmutation is actually taking place. But if you wish to consecrate a Life pattern with Prime 2, then you do need the relevant transmutation Life sphere because Life pattern quintessence is not static, it is constantly ebbing and flowing, so in order to the maintain the concecration to any degree of usability, locking it in with Life is required. </div> </div> </div>Wrong, wrong wrong and wrong. Show me any where in any of the editions that says that you need Life Sphere to consecrate living Patterns. I dare you.<br /> And you won't find any, because all that you need for consecration is Prime 2.<br /> And yes, I know what you are quoting. That entire part &quot;life patterns are not static...&quot; And so on, you're quoting (parafrasing) directly from the description of the Prime Sphere.<br /> And I can tell you that you won't find a single mention about it requiring Life Sphere, because that description has being the same pretty much since the 1st edition, and is also present in 2nd ed, rev and M20.<br /> And this description is what is used to justify why you need <b>Prime 2</b> to consecrate living Patterns rather than just Prime 1. Nowhere does it mention anything about needing Life - <i><u>because you're not manipulating living patterns at all.</u></i><br /> All that you are manipulating are the <b>ETHEREAL FLUCTUATIONS INSIDE OF A LIVING PATTERN</b>, but because living patterns are in constant flux, it is an operation more complex than manipulating the ethereal pattern of a matter pattern, hence why you need Prime 2 rather than 1.<br /> <br /> So yes, every single other Spheres in the game disprove what is written for in Correspondence. If you're manipulating the ethereal patterns of anything, ALL THAT YOU NEED IS PRIME.<br /> <br /> You just need to combine Spheres when you're TRANSMUTING a Pattern from one purview into another - for example, transmuting Quintessence into fire needs Prime and Forces; transmuting a lightning into a crazy silver sculpture needs Forces and Matter. Transmuting an imaginary friend into a Spiritual Chimera require Mind and Spirit.<br /> <br /> But, what lays between the purview of a single Sphere, can be manipulated by THAT SPHERE ALONE.<br /> <br /> Therefore, what is within the purview of Correspondence (manipulating &quot;Space&quot; or the &quot;Connections between patterns in that illusion we call Space&quot;) should be manipulated by Correspondence ALONE.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That is how the pattern spheres function, metaphysically all aspects of the spheres are flowing through them, all objects, living beings, and energies will have a Resonance on them (mind), a spiritual entite about them (Spirit), a place within the grander scheme of fate (Entropy), A level of quintessence allowing them to subsist in reality (Prime), a constant relationship with the (usually) forward march of time (Time) and a whole rolladex of connections to other objects, people, places, locations, memories, etc (Correspondence). </div> </div> </div>So why I don't need Matter 3 when I use Entropy 3 to break a machine? Why don't I need Life 3 when I use Time 3 to slow down somebody? I guess there's absolutely no example better than Time for that.<br /> <br /> Again, it doesn't make sense. Correspondence was just simply terribly written, and works differently to ANY other Sphere because of reasons.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-11T22:22:07-07:00","id":1538464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1537900#post1537900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> the idea or Correspondence as the sphere of connections is in the text for pretty much all editions, it stands above paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>No it doesn't. If you doubt me, go ready the Guide to the Technocracy about Correspondence to see if that holds true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-11T23:01:43-07:00","id":1538465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1537963#post1537963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You could argue that correspondence can be used to forge connections between objects, but in the same way that Resonance is an inherent part of a location once it is established, so are connections, and like resonance they come about from completely mundane interactions. I make the parallels with Fate, Spirit, and Mind to illustrate by, just how every object as a spirit that can be awakened with Spirit 3, a relationship with fate which can be tuned with Entropy 3 (whether you believe it to be how close to chaos it is, or how a part of destiny it is), and a resonance emanating from it which can be tuned with Mind 2 (or Prime), said objects also have connections. And when it comes to their environment, the strongest connections they have are the ones with the areas they are currently within, one of the reasons why line of sight is always the strongest connection, next to body sample.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bla bla bla, again, Prime 1 allows me to change the resonance of matter patterns, Prime 2 allows me to change the resonance of living Patterns and Mind 2 allows me to also change the resonance of places or objects. But I don't need to add Matter 2 to my Mind 2 effect to turn my yoga spa into a place that emanates peace and happiness, I just need Mind 2 for that. So again, Correspondence is still stupid, badly written and asinine-ly self contradictory.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I gave you a simple explanation, you didn't like it and seemed to think it was spurious. So I gave you my thoughts on it since I thought that would be of interest to you rather than dismissed as wasted effort. It is a little upsetting, but if you have decided I am wrong, then I must be wrong. </div> </div> </div>Oh comon. Don't take things personally.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Though for clarity, The simple explanation will be reiterated here:<br /> It has required Matter and Life for those effects in 2e, Revised, and in M20, this ruling being so consistent across multiple editions is pretty indicative that it has intended to work like this for a while. </div> </div> </div>Yes, and then it was immediately contradicted in all those editions, sometimes in the very same sentences.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Game design wise, the reason that it requires more spheres is because without said investment, Correspondence on its own becomes a bit...silly. Just 2 points in correspondence to teleport pretty much whatever you want wherever you like. An Arete 2 mage could pretty easily teleport an atomic bomb to whatever location they desire, rather than such a feat require Matter 5 Corr 5, (the level of matter required to transmute radioactive material without Forces) and thus be locked away until one becomes a master, at which point such a mage would have to be pretty dedicated to desire such a gambit. Similarly one could make the argument that you can start teleporting people &quot;if they are small enough&quot; with Corr 2. And when you can start teleporting people to and from yourself without any involvement of you in the process... no other sphere really need apply. So from a design perspective I would ask you to reconsider it as a house rule if you want any form of gravitas in your games to be maintained. But hey, some people like their mages gonzo, and who am I to tell you not to. I just can't personally recommend them. </div> </div> </div>Which is exactly why Correspondence is stupid to begin with. Tell me something: what's the difference between &quot;apporting&quot; an atomic bomb using Corr 5 and Matter 5 (which is stupid to begin with since with Matter 5 I can create my own bomb by whatever) to creating a portal with just Corr 4 right bellow that same bomb with the exit point of it inside my house?<br /> <br /> See just how stupid that game design is?<br /> <br /> That's why Apport is sooooooooooooo FUCKING STUPID. I'm sorry, but this is the dumbest effect of the entirety of Mage.<br /> <br /> To begin with, &quot;Apport&quot; is just simply TELEPORT.<br /> <br /> And teleportation is ALREADY CORRESPONDENCE 3.<br /> <br /> So, I can teleport myself anywhere with Correspondence 3, but I can't teleport other things to myself with it? Or I can't teleport Pattern A to Pattern (or point) B?<br /> <br /> WHAT KIND OF DUMB SHIT IS THIS?<br /> <br /> And secondly, yes, I fully agree that having an effect that allows teleportation at a mere rank 2 is stupid.<br /> <br /> ALLOWING TELEPORTATION AT RANK 2 IS STUPID.<br /> <b>*Hence why &quot;Apport&quot;, being a rank 2 effect, is so stupid</b><br /> <br /> And even more stupid when you realize that REAL (but not exactly) teleportion is Corr 3, which makes much more sense (but only for the Mage to teleport himself, which makes zero sense).<br /> <br /> Also, the entire &quot;must be something small&quot; is beyond just stupid, it verges the level of schizophrenic. What difference does it make if I teleport a coin or an airplane? The ONLY difference here should be in the number of successes, not in required level for the effect and much less about either or not it is possible.<br /> <br /> APPORT IS SOOOOOOOO STUPID!!!<br /> <br /> As for &quot;teleporting an A bomb with a rank 2 Sphere is stupid&quot; yeah, it absolutely is, which is why Teleportation is right where it should be as a rank 3 level Sphere rather than 2, and besides that, a nuke is not a small wallet, it would require tons of successes, it will be as vulgar as it gets and you can be sure that there will ALWAYS be a ton of witnesses, and if the Technocracy is worth a single dollar of their vast investments, they keep very close tabs on these sweet things, so good luck with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But in answer to the questions as being asked, this is how correspondence is written to work. I have addressed what is seen as a contradiction and explained my reasoning for why I believe this is the intended ruling out of the possible other interpretations. If you wish to ask clarification I am happy to further elaborate, otherwise by all means express your own reasoning for preferring your ruling. There is no reason either of us need convince the other of anything. The discussion is open for all to read and conclude as they best judge. </div> </div> </div>Except for the fact that it contradicts itself constantly and for the fact that it is so idiotic and stupid that I would rather castrate myself with a blunt knife than to ever adhere to that schizophrenic mess that is the description of apport.<br /> <br /> Again, if you want to understand just how stupid Apport is, just answer me why you don't need Life 3 in conjunction with Time 3 when you want to accelerate or slow somebody. I'll wait.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-12T07:16:43-07:00","id":1538476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1538460#post1538460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1 - Correspondence 2, Matter 2. If you're seeing the pin with a telescope, this is considered &quot;line of sight&quot; for the table of reach and difficulty.<br /> Edit: sorry, you asked for Corr alone. That would be Corr 4, just as all bellow.<br /> 2 - RAW you'd need Correspondence 4, but both this requirement and the requirement above are completely idiotic, and in my opinion, Correspondence is just simply awfully written, like so, so much stuff is in Mage.<br /> 3 - Corr 4 again, and again all the same considerations as above.<br /> 4 - Same as above.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why are you jumping up to Correspondence 4 for anything? All the objects listed are within the size range of Correspondence 2.<br /> <br /> Side note, that size limit seems very arbitrary as a limit on teleportation, but it makes a lot of sense as a limit of a range extension effect. What I mean is: picture the mage using his mundane ability of reaching out and grabbing the item or creature, just with Correspondence 2 to extend his range well, well beyond the length of his arm. This is admittedly still sketchy thinking when it comes to bringing the item back to himself and even the book has to describe it in teleportation terms. Nevertheless, its the best explanation I've come up with for the Small Item -&gt; Self -&gt; Other progression Correspondence uses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-12T10:11:46-07:00","id":1538482,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28035\" data-vbnamecard=\"28035\">Magus Maximus</a> I agree with the statements<i> &quot;Correspondence is one of the most horribly written Spheres out there&quot;</i> and <i>&quot;Correspondence was just simply terribly written, and works differently to ANY other Sphere because of reasons&quot;</i>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12193_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12193\" data-vbnamecard=\"12193\">Saikou</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> Appreciate your time and answers, but I think the questions are not solvable.<br /> <br /> <br /> I discovered late the Mage the Ascension, and... Man, it is hard to love. I like the merits/flaws, parts of the setting, but the mechanics? Horrible, I come to these forums thinking I can not be the only one who asked this, and maybe in the 30 or so years of lore, books and erratas, someone somewhere fixed those things. Don't even get me started on Consensus, whoever wrote that has probably not interacted with large number humans or has no idea what people believe in the USA and large parts of the world... If Consensus worked the Traditions should be WINNING! The Technocracy would be the underdogs! Most of the Bible belt would be managed literally on thoughts and prayers, and <i>it would work</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mage the Awakening is simply better, the mechanics and the way magic works is internally consistent and coherent, you can explain the effect in terms of practices at a certain level of skill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 07-12-2024, 11:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-12T10:57:29-07:00","id":1538483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1538482#post1538482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I can not be the only one who asked this, and maybe in the 30 or so years of lore, books and erratas, someone somewhere fixed those things.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mage the Awakening is simply better, the mechanics and the way magic works is internally consistent and coherent, you can explain the effect in terms of practices at a certain level of skill.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ramnesis had a topic where he scrolled the m20 rulebook sphere by sphere fixing them but sadly never finished.<br /> <br /> As for Mtaw strongly dissagree. Its more consistent but also far more limiting.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-12T12:27:16-07:00","id":1538486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1538483#post1538483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ramnesis had a topic where he scrolled the m20 rulebook sphere by sphere fixing them but sadly never finished.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well I wasn't so much fixing them as highlighting when M20 contradicted itself and stating which version I thought was correct. It's only on hiatus right now. I started trying to do the same thing for HDYDT and it depressed me to the point of killing my motivation. This isn't one of my usual cracks about HDYDT either, actually deep diving into it is really draining. <br /> <br /> Anyways, the Matter list for M20 is mostly complete and after that there is just Time and Mind, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-13T11:14:48-07:00","id":1538530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1538482#post1538482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28035\" data-vbnamecard=\"28035\">Magus Maximus</a> I agree with the statements<i> &quot;Correspondence is one of the most horribly written Spheres out there&quot;</i> and <i>&quot;Correspondence was just simply terribly written, and works differently to ANY other Sphere because of reasons&quot;</i>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12193_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12193\" data-vbnamecard=\"12193\">Saikou</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> Appreciate your time and answers, but I think the questions are not solvable.<br /> <br /> <br /> I discovered late the Mage the Ascension, and... Man, it is hard to love. I like the merits/flaws, parts of the setting, but the mechanics? Horrible, I come to these forums thinking I can not be the only one who asked this, and maybe in the 30 or so years of lore, books and erratas, someone somewhere fixed those things. Don't even get me started on Consensus, whoever wrote that has probably not interacted with large number humans or has no idea what people believe in the USA and large parts of the world... If Consensus worked the Traditions should be WINNING! The Technocracy would be the underdogs! Most of the Bible belt would be managed literally on thoughts and prayers, and <i>it would work</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mage the Awakening is simply better, the mechanics and the way magic works is internally consistent and coherent, you can explain the effect in terms of practices at a certain level of skill.</div> </div> </div> </div>I gave up on the idea of Consensus long ago, and decided to just go with it, and that the WoD Mage isn't truly a reflection of our own, and that people's &quot;faith&quot; in WoD is more like apathy towards something more archetypical... So they have &quot;faith&quot; in the &quot;archetype of Jesus&quot; or the &quot;archetype of Allah&quot; or the &quot;archetype of Shiva&quot; rather than actually believing in angels and in Satan or Shaitan <br /> <br /> In a way, that serves the setting well - decadent, cynical and hypocritical societies - but it is NOT a reflection of our world. Because in our world, the majority of people DO believe in angels and demons and djins and kamis and rakshasas and what not, and not just as mere concepts or metaphors or archetypes.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, while I think nobody believes that electricity is witchcraft, 99% of people just accept it as a fact of life without having any idea of how it works, and you also have people that believe that Evolution and even the roundness of Earth are CIA conspiracies, so no, I would never say that &quot;da sCience&quot; is the prevailing Paradigm - not to mention the infection of biased views and post modernist insanity in science nowadays, and the ton of pseudoscience that proliferates.<br /> <br /> Yeah, you're not alone in that assessment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-13T16:11:55-07:00","id":1538545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1538530#post1538530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I gave up on the idea of Consensus long ago, and decided to just go with it, and that the WoD Mage isn't truly a reflection of our own, and that people's &quot;faith&quot; in WoD is more like apathy towards something more archetypical... So they have &quot;faith&quot; in the &quot;archetype of Jesus&quot; or the &quot;archetype of Allah&quot; or the &quot;archetype of Shiva&quot; rather than actually believing in angels and in Satan or Shaitan<br /> <br /> In a way, that serves the setting well - decadent, cynical and hypocritical societies - but it is NOT a reflection of our world. Because in our world, the majority of people DO believe in angels and demons and djins and kamis and rakshasas and what not, and not just as mere concepts or metaphors or archetypes.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, while I think nobody believes that electricity is witchcraft, 99% of people just accept it as a fact of life without having any idea of how it works, and you also have people that believe that Evolution and even the roundness of Earth are CIA conspiracies, so no, I would never say that &quot;da sCience&quot; is the prevailing Paradigm - not to mention the infection of biased views and post modernist insanity in science nowadays, and the ton of pseudoscience that proliferates.<br /> <br /> Yeah, you're not alone in that assessment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quoted for truth.<br /> <br /> My brother from another mother.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-14T02:55:04-07:00","id":1538556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1538465#post1538465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bla bla bla, again, Prime 1 allows me to change the resonance of matter patterns, Prime 2 allows me to change the resonance of living Patterns and Mind 2 allows me to also change the resonance of places or objects. But I don't need to add Matter 2 to my Mind 2 effect to turn my yoga spa into a place that emanates peace and happiness, I just need Mind 2 for that. So again, Correspondence is still stupid, badly written and asinine-ly self contradictory.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can with correspondence alone change the connection of objects, this would be the equivalent of using Mind magic to alter the resonance of objects. (and as an aside, it would be Prime 2 to place it on objects.<br /> You do need Matter 2 if you want to lock effects on to matter patterns, such as an effect which causes light to change as it approaches the object.<br /> <br /> The conclusion that correspondence is self contradictory, however, falls a bit flat if you are comparing it to other spheres.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1538465#post1538465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, and then it was immediately contradicted in all those editions, sometimes in the very same sentences.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll need to source that for 2e and revised as I do not see these contradictions.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1538465#post1538465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is exactly why Correspondence is stupid to begin with. Tell me something: what's the difference between &quot;apporting&quot; an atomic bomb using Corr 5 and Matter 5 (which is stupid to begin with since with Matter 5 I can create my own bomb by whatever) to creating a portal with just Corr 4 right bellow that same bomb with the exit point of it inside my house.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>In theory you can with Matter 5 create an atom bomb, but you would both need to know how to make it, and the feat would be far more complicated, and as a result far more risky, than take a ready made bomb and using that. Creating is a difficult thing which requires a great deal of quintessence if made from nothing, especially when making something as unstable as a nuclear weapon. And again if you do not have sufficient knowledge of nuclear physics, nuclear weapons, or other elements of the devices, such a thing will be beyond your capability to create.<br /> <br /> The difference between Apportation and creating a portal is that, if you create a portal you need to physically walk over the threshold, grab what you need, and bring it back across. Your portal will need to be big enough to accommodate what it is you mean to transfer, and said portal would be far more likely to be vulgar as it is much more difficult to disguise a gateway than it is to disguise an object going missing. We could argue hypotheticals about surveillance, but the point isn't whether or not both can be considered vulgar, just that portals are, on the whole, more likely to be vulgar in general.<br /> <br /> Apportation instead is when the object is now with you, rather than where it was. You don't have to cross the space, the object does all the crossing. It is changes location. Much more difficult to tie you to the taking.<br /> <br /> Though a lot more work, you can also use apportation to change the location of an object to another location that is not with you. Now you could make a gate between two different locations that are not with you, but if you are not there to go through the gate, very little will actually shift through it. Not without other spheres anyway to change momentum across the distances or influence circumstance such that the object will simply drop through the portals, all of which are possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1538465#post1538465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> <br /> See just how stupid that game design is?<br /> <br /> That's why Apport is sooooooooooooo FUCKING STUPID. I'm sorry, but this is the dumbest effect of the entirety of Mage.<br /> <br /> To begin with, &quot;Apport&quot; is just simply TELEPORT.<br /> <br /> And teleportation is ALREADY CORRESPONDENCE 3.<br /> <br /> So, I can teleport myself anywhere with Correspondence 3, but I can't teleport other things to myself with it? Or I can't teleport Pattern A to Pattern (or point) B?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this is a common theme in Mage, it is far easier to affect the self than it is to affect others. This is why Life effects can apply to yourself at a lower rank than they apply to others, why Mind 1 is sufficient to expand your senses to increase mental traits but a higher rank of Mind is required to do this in others. Affecting that which is not in yourself requires an additional success on the roll. This is simply another manifestation of this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1538465#post1538465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And secondly, yes, I fully agree that having an effect that allows teleportation at a mere rank 2 is stupid.<br /> <br /> ALLOWING TELEPORTATION AT RANK 2 IS STUPID.<br /> <b>*Hence why &quot;Apport&quot;, being a rank 2 effect, is so stupid</b><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The idea is that at Correspondence 2, you can send out your senses, including your sense of touch to hold an object and feel it. And extension of that ability to touch if to pull it towards you, make it so that connection of touch which is sensory is now manifest to the object itself, placing it in your hand. That extension of the ability is done by having that understanding of matter, such that you can extend your senses to the object itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1538465#post1538465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> <br /> And even more stupid when you realize that REAL (but not exactly) teleportion is Corr 3, which makes much more sense (but only for the Mage to teleport himself, which makes zero sense).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Again, it makes sense, it is yet another example of effects being easier to do to yourself than it is to do to others. You can affect your connections better than another's connections.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1538465#post1538465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> <br /> Also, the entire &quot;must be something small&quot; is beyond just stupid, it verges the level of schizophrenic. What difference does it make if I teleport a coin or an airplane? The ONLY difference here should be in the number of successes, not in required level for the effect and much less about either or not it is possible.<br /> <br /> APPORT IS SOOOOOOOO STUPID!!!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There is no need to be hyperbolic. The scale of effect is something which if reflected in other spheres as well. No matter how many successes you get with a Forces 2 effect, you will not be able to affect the weather. No matter how many successes you get with a Life 3 effect, you will not be able to transform in to an animal, and no matter how many successes you get with a Prime 3 effect, you will not be able to completely remove all from an object that is not Tass, as such requires Prime 5. This is consistent with the way the spheres work, certain feats are simply beyond the capabilities of the lower ranks, and are unable to achieve these godlike capabilities.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1538465#post1538465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> <br /> As for &quot;teleporting an A bomb with a rank 2 Sphere is stupid&quot; yeah, it absolutely is, which is why Teleportation is right where it should be as a rank 3 level Sphere rather than 2, and besides that, a nuke is not a small wallet, it would require tons of successes, it will be as vulgar as it gets and you can be sure that there will ALWAYS be a ton of witnesses, and if the Technocracy is worth a single dollar of their vast investments, they keep very close tabs on these sweet things, so good luck with that.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Discussions of vulgarity start to go towards hypothetical scenarios, so I will avoid distracting the point that getting to embroiled with this.<br /> <br /> If you wished, you could make it that without Matter it is prohibitively difficult to teleport a complex object, but make it far easier if you have the appropriate rank in matter. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1538465#post1538465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> <br /> Except for the fact that it contradicts itself constantly and for the fact that it is so idiotic and stupid that I would rather castrate myself with a blunt knife than to ever adhere to that schizophrenic mess that is the description of apport.<br /> <br /> Again, if you want to understand just how stupid Apport is, just answer me why you don't need Life 3 in conjunction with Time 3 when you want to accelerate or slow somebody. I'll wait.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, you do. Time 3 alone works on areas, as does Forces. You can use your Focus to keep the effect up with you as you move around, as you can with Forces, or you can lock it in to a pattern, such as Matter to lock it in to a gem so as to not need to actively concentrate on the effect, or allow another the benefit of the effect. If you wish to accelerate a specific person's body, such as your own body to speed up healing time, you would need Time 3 with Life 2 as well. This can be a preferable way to deal with Aggravated damage as it does not require quintessence to heal. This is also the case for reversing time, where if you reverse time you are creating a small bubble of events which go backwards, but if you mix in Life 3 you can reverse yourself through time, not just within the bubble, but to, for example, restart your day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-14T03:03:18-07:00","id":1538557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1538482#post1538482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28035\" data-vbnamecard=\"28035\">Magus Maximus</a> I agree with the statements<i> &quot;Correspondence is one of the most horribly written Spheres out there&quot;</i> and <i>&quot;Correspondence was just simply terribly written, and works differently to ANY other Sphere because of reasons&quot;</i>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12193_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12193\" data-vbnamecard=\"12193\">Saikou</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> Appreciate your time and answers, but I think the questions are not solvable.<br /> <br /> <br /> I discovered late the Mage the Ascension, and... Man, it is hard to love. I like the merits/flaws, parts of the setting, but the mechanics? Horrible, I come to these forums thinking I can not be the only one who asked this, and maybe in the 30 or so years of lore, books and erratas, someone somewhere fixed those things. Don't even get me started on Consensus, whoever wrote that has probably not interacted with large number humans or has no idea what people believe in the USA and large parts of the world... If Consensus worked the Traditions should be WINNING! The Technocracy would be the underdogs! Most of the Bible belt would be managed literally on thoughts and prayers, and <i>it would work</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mage the Awakening is simply better, the mechanics and the way magic works is internally consistent and coherent, you can explain the effect in terms of practices at a certain level of skill.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I find Awakening to be......not all it's advertised to be<br /> <br /> I have yet to have an ST run it in a way that didn't make me feel horribly constrained. One even told me that My Moros character, who is a woman grieving for the loss of her husband and so became obsessed with death, Shouldn't be a Moros because they beleived, as they were Japanese, that they would naturally become an exorcist, and thus should instead have a higher affinity with Spirits than Moros allows, my character was not optimal and thus not worth having.<br /> <br /> Another I asked if I could use Space 1 effect Correspondence to learn the origin of a magic item, they told me no because &quot;it is from the supernal realms and Space can't really touch that, that is a Prime thing&quot;, but when I told them I also have Prime 1, they just froze, unsure how to handle the situation, telling me they were super reluctant to allow it because it means &quot;I could just use Space in every effect to get bonuses if this was allowed&quot;<br /> <br /> I never have these issues with Ascension, it's a case of &quot;Does what you're doing make sense&quot; if so, then yes, if not then let's see what would make sense and do that instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-14T09:20:23-07:00","id":1538566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1538557#post1538557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally I find Awakening to be......not all it's advertised to be<br /> <br /> I have yet to have an ST run it in a way that didn't make me feel horribly constrained. One even told me that My Moros character, who is a woman grieving for the loss of her husband and so became obsessed with death, Shouldn't be a Moros because they beleived, as they were Japanese, that they would naturally become an exorcist, and thus should instead have a higher affinity with Spirits than Moros allows, my character was not optimal and thus not worth having.<br /> <br /> Another I asked if I could use Space 1 effect Correspondence to learn the origin of a magic item, they told me no because &quot;it is from the supernal realms and Space can't really touch that, that is a Prime thing&quot;, but when I told them I also have Prime 1, they just froze, unsure how to handle the situation, telling me they were super reluctant to allow it because it means &quot;I could just use Space in every effect to get bonuses if this was allowed&quot;<br /> <br /> I never have these issues with Ascension, it's a case of &quot;Does what you're doing make sense&quot; if so, then yes, if not then let's see what would make sense and do that instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of these read like you had some ST that do not know the rules and/or lack experience more than the rules being bad.<br /> <br /> My comparison was about the rules as written and designed have gaps and glaring faults in Ascension (otherwise there would not be so many rules questions) and it was never designed with a full vision, versus the new world of darkness where everyone uses the mortal rules to start and on top you add the templates, so crossoverss are feasible and reasonable. In the specific case of Awakening's magic system, the rules are clear, structured and built upon the previous levels so even if you disagree with the result it is never contradictory what can or can not be done by an Arcana at certain rank.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-14T09:42:32-07:00","id":1538567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1538566#post1538566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All of these read like you had some ST that do not know the rules and/or lack experience more than the rules being bad.<br /> <br /> My comparison was about the rules as written and designed have gaps and glaring faults in Ascension (otherwise there would not be so many rules questions) and it was never designed with a full vision, versus the new world of darkness where everyone uses the mortal rules to start and on top you add the templates, so crossoverss are feasible and reasonable. In the specific case of Awakening's magic system, the rules are clear, structured and built upon the previous levels so even if you disagree with the result it is never contradictory what can or can not be done by an Arcana at certain rank.</div> </div> </div> </div>my STs were plenty familiar with Awakening, they just didn't know how to handle my approach to making characters or effects for it. Which seems to be a consistent problem in how Awakening works vs how it\u2019s advertised to work. Everyone says it\u2019s less ST dependent, but my goodness I have found this to be the direct opposite. Any time I did creative thaumaturgy, my STs typically either pointed me to the spell lists and said \u201cunless it\u2019s in there, no can do\u201d or \u201cmaybe\u2026but I think that\u2019s actually 2 separate effects\u201d or \u201cyes, I can create a condition for that\u201d or \u201cum\u2026.That might be a Weaving effect instead of a Ruling effect (which, by the way is never clearly defined what the difference is between these practices are). So yes, much rule dispute<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve also found that Awakening lacks in any info on how to use conjunctive effects. So many times I have tried to combine arcana and been told \u201cit doesn\u2019t say you can on the example, so no\u201d or \u201cthose are two separate effects so you must cast them individually\u201d<br /> <br /> Often the dismissive counter is \u201coh, but Awakening doesn\u2019t need conjunctive effects, you can do so many things with just one arcanaum.\u201d And I\u2019m like, I had Death and Mind, let me know what the heck having both of these does for me. If I can\u2019t read the minds of ghosts or cause someone\u2019s senses to fall towards the shadows, giving them the death sense I have, then why even lie? There is no combining, it\u2019s just unlocking new spells on your spell list.<br /> <br /> even the creative thaumaturgy works like this. It\u2019s just unlocking which conditions or tilts you can now apply on to people\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-14T23:04:21-07:00","id":1538595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1538556#post1538556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can with correspondence alone change the connection of objects, this would be the equivalent of using Mind magic to alter the resonance of objects. (and as an aside, it would be Prime 2 to place it on objects.<br /> You do need Matter 2 if you want to lock effects on to matter patterns, such as an effect which causes light to change as it approaches the object.</div> </div> </div> </div>Errr... No, you do not.<br /> <br /> Mind 2 you can create a doll that emanates peace and happiness to gift to a child... And you just need Mind 2 for that. No requirements at all for Matter.<br /> <br /> If that was the case, Mind would become a very silly Sphere, if then you'd decide that you always need to add Life in order to make any sort of alterations into somebody's mind.<br /> <br /> Do you want to mind ready? Yeah, Mind 3 + Life (2? 3? Who knows)<br /> <br /> Do you want to alter memories? Mind 4 + some random Life lvl<br /> <br /> That's not how it works, and that's not how it should work.<br /> <br /> Likewise, it is absolutely terrible that Correspondence requires other Spheres that add nothing to an effect that is 100% within the purview of Corr itself. Aport is teleportation, simple as that, and that is a measure of space manipulation. Sure, we could go on with the interpretation of &quot;Connections&quot; and that all space is same space (thus everything is an illusion basically), but aside that this is ONE among many possible Paradigms, it doesn't change the fact that is &quot;space&quot; manipulation, or if you prefer it in other words, it is the manipulation of the &quot;Connections&quot;, and therefore, if Corr is the Sphere of Connections, than &quot;teleportation&quot; (or if you prefer, the &quot;reassignment of points of connection&quot;), then it is still within the full purview of Correspondence and Correspondence alone, thus no other Spheres should be involved.<br /> <br /> In the case of &quot;light bending over in an object&quot;, this could be done with Forces 2 Matter 2; fair enough, but there is actually a reason for it, it's not just randomly placed on the effect and it's not because you &quot;always need Matter or Life to affect patterns with any other Spheres&quot;, because that declaration is in itself false, since you don't need neither Life nor Matter for Mind, Prime, Entropy, Time and many other effects.<br /> <br /> No, the reason why you need Forces and Matter is because you're adding a Forces effect into a matter pattern. Matter patterns don't usually possess forces patterns by themselves. It's much like the same reason as to why you would need Forces 5 and Life 5 if you want to turn into a living lightning bolt, or Matter 5 Life 5 if you want to turn into a living statue. You're mixing both parameters, making something that combine both purviews.<br /> <br /> You don't need Matter in order to manipulate the resonance inside of a matter pattern thou, because resonance is something present in all patterns but they do NOT affect the material composition of the Pattern. Changing the resonance of a hammer won't affect the hammer. It may affect how people perceive the hammer, but it won't change how the material hammer interacts with the material world. Changing the resonance of the hammer won't make it glow in the dark, it won't make it heavier or softer and won't make it attract metals like a magnet. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The conclusion that correspondence is self contradictory, however, falls a bit flat if you are comparing it to other spheres. </div> </div> </div>Only because practically all other Spheres are just as messy as it<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You'll need to source that for 2e and revised as I do not see these contradictions. </div> </div> </div>If I ever have time in my life (my 4 months baby just went to sleep and it's 1:50 am here) I'll try to find it, but there's a 99.99% chance I'll never have the change, not gonna lie.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In theory you can with Matter 5 create an atom bomb, but you would both need to know how to make it, and the feat would be far more complicated, and as a result far more risky, than take a ready made bomb and using that. Creating is a difficult thing which requires a great deal of quintessence if made from nothing, especially when making something as unstable as a nuclear weapon. And again if you do not have sufficient knowledge of nuclear physics, nuclear weapons, or other elements of the devices, such a thing will be beyond your capability to create. </div> </div> </div>Not true at all. Being a PhD in nuclear physics surely would be, no doubt, but if your purpose is &quot;just&quot; to &quot;make stuff that goes bum bum&quot;, you really don't need that. And neither do you need to adhere to &quot;technocratic paradigm&quot; either. You can just as well go for the &quot;mythical hellfire&quot; stuff.<br /> <br /> Besides, people say this as if it were that hard. Man, you can find information about how to build an A bomb on the internet. It's actually not hard at all, in just another 20 more years this technology will be a century old (yeah, WW2 is rapidly becoming &quot;ancient history&quot;, believe it or not).<br /> <br /> The hard part is getting enriched nuclear material. That's what's hard to get. You need some heavy industry for that, and precision equipment for the centrifuges.<br /> <br /> But guess what? Matter 5 can do that hard part (enriched uranium) with &quot;easy&quot;. And enriched uranium is not hard at all to understand, you just need to look at a periodic table and have some basic chemistry knowledge to know it is the Uranium 235 isotope that you need.<br /> <br /> After you get a few kilograms (or pounds) of it, making a bomb is secondary.<br /> <br /> Now, if even that basic knowledge you lack, you can:<br /> Use Mind 4 on a Nuclear Physicist professor and &quot;download&quot; the knowledge directly or;<br /> Use Entropy 5 to &quot;download the knowledge directly from the Cosmos&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The difference between Apportation and creating a portal is that, if you create a portal you need to physically walk over the threshold, grab what you need, and bring it back across. Your portal will need to be big enough to accommodate what it is you mean to transfer, and said portal would be far more likely to be vulgar as it is much more difficult to disguise a gateway than it is to disguise an object going missing. We could argue hypotheticals about surveillance, but the point isn't whether or not both can be considered vulgar, just that portals are, on the whole, more likely to be vulgar in general. </div> </div> </div>No, you don't need to grab anything. You can just create the portal immediately bellow the object of your heist and let gravity do the rest. Or you can even make your portal move towards the object and &quot;swallow&quot; it.<br /> <br /> Besides, both actions are equally vulgar, except perhaps in Looney town, were portable holes are a thing. Anywhere else in the material world, it will always be vulgar (except in your sanctum or lab)<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Apportation instead is when the object is now with you, rather than where it was. You don't have to cross the space, the object does all the crossing. It is changes location. Much more difficult to tie you to the taking. </div> </div> </div>This almost seems like debating semantics. It doesn't matter. A portal will do the exact same, and if you go Looney Tunes placing the portal bellow the object, or &quot;throwing&quot; the portal at it, it has the exact same effect, with the object coming to you just the same.<br /> <br /> And if anyone is paying any attention, they'll notice that the object is no longer there just the same. And unless the ones guarding it also have Correspondence, they won't be able to trace the heist to you regardless. And if they DO have Correspondence, they WILL find you just the same.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Though a lot more work, you can also use apportation to change the location of an object to another location that is not with you. Now you could make a gate between two different locations that are not with you, but if you are not there to go through the gate, very little will actually shift through it. Not without other spheres anyway to change momentum across the distances or influence circumstance such that the object will simply drop through the portals, all of which are possible. </div> </div> </div>Not true at all. Correspondence 4 isn't just creating portals, it is also manipulating Space, shrinking or enlarging it at will.<br /> <br /> As such, you can actually use it for a sort of &quot;telekinesis&quot; effect, but you won't actually be moving the object by application of energy, but rather by manipulating the space around it. You can, for example, make someone &quot;fly&quot; by enlarging the space between that person's shoes and the ground from millimeters to kilometers (or from 0.1 inches to miles). <br /> <br /> Besides, &quot;Apport&quot; is stupid in itself by the simple fact that Teleportation is already Corr 3, and Apport is just teleportation. It is nothing more and nothing less than teleportation. So it's stupid to have the same effect at a lower level and even more stupid that it requires other Spheres that have nothing to do with Space manipulation and even more stupid that it has a SIZE LIMITATION attached to the SPHERE THAT MANIPULATES SPACE.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, this is a common theme in Mage, it is far easier to affect the self than it is to affect others. This is why Life effects can apply to yourself at a lower rank than they apply to others, why Mind 1 is sufficient to expand your senses to increase mental traits but a higher rank of Mind is required to do this in others. Affecting that which is not in yourself requires an additional success on the roll. This is simply another manifestation of this. </div> </div> </div>Yes, and I already said plenty of times that this is beyond stupid in the case of Life. You can do stuff that requires Life 3, but in yourself it only requires Life 2 because of reasons?<br /> In the case of Mind, it makes total sense. You actually can change your own mind without even needing to use Magik - heck, you don't even need to be a Mage, you just need the will to change your own thoughts. So of course it should be more direct - you are, after all, in direct contact with your own mind, and the very act of working a Magik effect comes from your own thoughts. So in the case of Mind it makes perfect sense.<br /> <br /> As for the &quot;any other targets requires an additional success&quot;, yes, that makes sense too. And that is all that is needed to make effects upon the self being easier, NOT randomly setting lower lvl requirements for Spheres. And specially, for Correspondence that is utterly stupid. You can't increase your own luck with just Entropy 1; neither can you &quot;bless&quot; yourself with a more fit body with just Entropy 3. And you can't accelerate yourself with Time 2 alone.<br /> <br /> So, tell you what, how about we start letting Mages accelerate themselves with Time 2 alone? Seriously, why not thou? Would it be a little OP and unbalanced? Ohhhh yes... That's right.<br /> <br /> But let's make something clear... Time and Correspondence are actually pretty similar Spheres, or close Spheres. To the point that &quot;da sCience&quot; claims it to be the same thing. Even mystic views claim both to be &quot;illusions of the senses&quot;. So, why are the rules for Correspondence, but not for Time? Why can't a Mage time travel himself with Time 4 alone?<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> [Quote]The idea is that at Correspondence 2, you can send out your senses, including your sense of touch to hold an object and feel it. And extension of that ability to touch if to pull it towards you, make it so that connection of touch which is sensory is now manifest to the object itself, placing it in your hand. That extension of the ability is done by having that understanding of matter, such that you can extend your senses to the object itself.[\\quote]<br /> Total non sequitur. You're not seeing stuff far away because you cast a &quot;wizard eye&quot; like in D&amp;D were you summon an actual floating eye. You're not transposing your eyes or your ears to a different location. Just your senses. Likewise, you're not really touching anything, you're just transporting your sense of touch somewhere else. So no, one thing does not mean you can actually grab those.<br /> And not, what you're referring here is the &quot;scrying&quot; effect, not the Apport. Apport is still stupid.<br /> <br /> Besides, that still doesn't explain at all why other Spheres are needed, you're just using circular argument and non sequitur <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, it makes sense, it is yet another example of effects being easier to do to yourself than it is to do to others. You can affect your connections better than another's connections. </div> </div> </div>Yes, that is reflected in the table for required successes, where you don't need an extra effect to affect yourself. No need for it to be arbitrarily a level bellow effect.<br /> <br /> Again, Entropy doesn't have it, Time doesn't have it. Only Correspondence have this &quot;because of reasons&quot;. If you could Teleport yourself alone with Corr 3 but needs Corr 4 for others, than you also should need Time 2 to accelerate yourself, or Entropy 3 to &quot;bless&quot; your own body. Forgive me, but that's just awful writing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is no need to be hyperbolic. The scale of effect is something which if reflected in other spheres as well. No matter how many successes you get with a Forces 2 effect, you will not be able to affect the weather. No matter how many successes you get with a Life 3 effect, you will not be able to transform in to an animal, and no matter how many successes you get with a Prime 3 effect, you will not be able to completely remove all from an object that is not Tass, as such requires Prime 5. This is consistent with the way the spheres work, certain feats are simply beyond the capabilities of the lower ranks, and are unable to achieve these godlike capabilities. </div> </div> </div>THANK YOU!! YES, EXACTLY!<br /> <br /> Indeed, I have for many years said that Forces is the dumbest, most idiotic of all the Spheres - and boy, Forces manages to get that title despite the fierce competition.<br /> <br /> Forces is ABSOLUTELY MORONIC.<br /> <br /> What's the difference between a breeze and a hurricane?<br /> <br /> What's the difference between vibrating the walls and an earthquake?<br /> <br /> WHERE DOES <b>LOWER FORCES </b>AND <b>HIGHER FORCES</b> BEGIN OR END?<br /> <br /> If you go into Ramnesis topic where we discuss all of the dumbery about the Spheres, you'll find my rant about Forces right there. It is beyond just stupid. It is completely asinine, because there's no possible parameter that can be used to differentiate between &quot;lower&quot; and &quot;higher&quot; forces.<br /> <br /> Besides, difference in magnitude of effects is already covered on AMOUNT OF SUCCESSES REQUIRED.<br /> <br /> To ALL Spheres, what differentiates one level from another is not &quot;my dick is bigger than thou&quot;, but rather the COMPLEXITY OF A PROCCESS.<br /> <br /> For instance, Mind 4 allows to create or erase memories. Mind 5 is not &quot;create or erase memories, but more, more, more!&quot;. No, Mind 5 is CREATE A NEW MIND.<br /> <br /> Do you want to create an AGI? (Artificial General Intelligence) Mind 5.<br /> <br /> You can Astral Travel with Mind 4, but you're constraint by your Silver Cord. With Mind 5 you don't &quot;Astral Travel for longer&quot;. No, it allows you to disconnect your mind from your body completely and to exist as a pure mental construct, and perhaps possess an entirely new body. It's a totally different power.<br /> <br /> Your other examples prove how dumb both Corr and mostly of all, Forces, are. Yes, you CANNOT turn into an animal with Life 3. Why? Because that is a more COMPLEX operation. It is NOT a matter of scale, but rather of complexity. As for Prime 3, I'm assuming you're talking about &quot;disintegrating&quot; something into it's formative Quintessence? If that's so, yes, exactly, because &quot;dissipating&quot; something into pure Quintessence is NOT something that requires a bigger scale than sucking the Quint from a Tass, but it rather a matter of complexity. The Quint in a Tass is still Quint; it's just &quot;frozen&quot; inside of a patter.<br /> On the other hand thou, a material pattern does not have any &quot;free&quot; Quint in it; whatever Quint it has, is already in its &quot;used&quot; form, and thus it is a far more complex procedure to revert it back from material to ethereal, rather than just freeing the ether that is just trapped inside but not &quot;converted&quot;.<br /> <br /> Do you want to know just how stupid Forces is? Very well. I'll give you an example that will kill any of your doubts and arguments, and show exactly how this works: I can turn an entire castle into sand with just Matter 2. Or I could turn an entire tsunami into gelatin. The only problem is that I will need way more than 20 successes for that.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, if I want to create 1 pound of Mithril or Vibranium or Adamatium or Unobtainium, I need Matter 5 and way less successes than to turn the oceans into gelatin. That, is COMPLEXITY.<br /> <br /> Scale vs Complexity. Scale is a matter of successes, Complexity is a matter of adequate level. That's how all the (more or less) functional spheres work. The exceptions are the dumb King and dumb Queen of the Spheres, respectfully Forces and Correspondence.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually, you do. Time 3 alone works on areas, as does Forces. You can use your Focus to keep the effect up with you as you move around, as you can with Forces, or you can lock it in to a pattern, such as Matter to lock it in to a gem so as to not need to actively concentrate on the effect, or allow another the benefit of the effect. If you wish to accelerate a specific person's body, such as your own body to speed up healing time, you would need Time 3 with Life 2 as well. This can be a preferable way to deal with Aggravated damage as it does not require quintessence to heal. This is also the case for reversing time, where if you reverse time you are creating a small bubble of events which go backwards, but if you mix in Life 3 you can reverse yourself through time, not just within the bubble, but to, for example, restart your day. </div> </div> </div>No, you don't. AT ALL. That's what the &quot;requires one extra success per target other than self&quot; is for.<br /> <br /> And, you don't need Time AT ALL to accelerate metabolism or &quot;reverse aging&quot;. You can do it with Life alone, and now you're doing the same mistake that the writers do to add Spheres because &quot;it feels right&quot;. Don't do this, only ever add an Sphere if it actually deals with something that requires its purview and only if strictly necessary.<br /> <br /> And Time 3 don't allow you to &quot;restart your day&quot;. In order to &quot;redo time&quot; you need Time 4, and that only allows for a single turn per success... So in order to &quot;restart your day&quot; you would need an ungodly amount of successes (considering that each hour has 3600 seconds, good luck with that). And Time travelling to the past has being restricted to arch-mastery.<br /> <br /> And you don't need Life AT ALL for ANY EFFECTS USING TIME. In absolutely NO WHERE is ever written so. And neither should it be.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-14T23:07:11-07:00","id":1538596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1538557#post1538557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally I find Awakening to be......not all it's advertised to be<br /> <br /> I have yet to have an ST run it in a way that didn't make me feel horribly constrained. One even told me that My Moros character, who is a woman grieving for the loss of her husband and so became obsessed with death, Shouldn't be a Moros because they beleived, as they were Japanese, that they would naturally become an exorcist, and thus should instead have a higher affinity with Spirits than Moros allows, my character was not optimal and thus not worth having.<br /> <br /> Another I asked if I could use Space 1 effect Correspondence to learn the origin of a magic item, they told me no because &quot;it is from the supernal realms and Space can't really touch that, that is a Prime thing&quot;, but when I told them I also have Prime 1, they just froze, unsure how to handle the situation, telling me they were super reluctant to allow it because it means &quot;I could just use Space in every effect to get bonuses if this was allowed&quot;<br /> <br /> I never have these issues with Ascension, it's a case of &quot;Does what you're doing make sense&quot; if so, then yes, if not then let's see what would make sense and do that instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I don't care about Awakening one bit. All that is necessary is for taking the dumb out of Ascension and it is fine, but Awakening made too huge an effort to be consistent, to the point that it became nonsensical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-15T00:27:36-07:00","id":1538600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1538596#post1538596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. I don't care about Awakening one bit. All that is necessary is for taking the dumb out of Ascension and it is fine, but Awakening made too huge an effort to be consistent, to the point that it became nonsensical.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you elaborate? I have my own grivences with it being too artificial but i would like to know your opinion.<br /> <br /> As for forces i go:<br /> 1. Sight/Sense<br /> 2. Control existing minor forces (heat, sound, preasure, kinetic energy)<br /> 3. Create minor forces, control Major forces (Electromegnetism, gravity, radiation)<br /> 4. Create major forces<br /> 5. Create complex forcess efects that combine multiple forces like fire tornadoes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-15T01:59:29-07:00","id":1538601,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28035\" data-vbnamecard=\"28035\">Magus Maximus</a><br /> you\u2019ve written too much for me to reply to individually. But my impression is that you have essentially house rulled the majority of how the spheres function, or have played with an ST who has house rulled how the spheres function and don\u2019t actually have a solid grasp of the RAW itself. Either that or you are quite drastically missing much of what I am saying.<br /> <br /> It might be more productive to continue this in a VC style setting where ideas can be properly exchanged and I can be sure we have a chance to listen to what we intend to say rather than go off on what we believe the other to have said, as do often happens in text.<br /> <br /> but as it stands, based on how much of your complaints are either refuting things which are RAW, disliking elements which have been thr case across all editions, and how you have contradicted me as I quoted from the boom itself, especially regarding locking to a pattern, my impression is you don\u2019t have a firm understanding of the rules as written in these books. You have a firm understanding of how it works in your head, but when something in the book challenges that, rather than reevaluate your personal understanding, you just decide since it does not fit, and so makes sense to you, it simply doesn\u2019t make sense at all, therefore it cannot make sense at all.<br /> <br /> the system as written however makes a lot of sense to me. And I was hoping to provide you why it was that it did make sense, and how I come to use it. But as most of your counters amount to \u201cno, I\u2019m right and here's all the reasons you are wrong\u201d which\u2026 doesn\u2019t really leave much room for attempts to understand one another.<br /> <br /> you are of course free to have your own internal model for the game, and use that in favour of written material. But then I believe it is rather unecessary to then say everyone else who understands the system and promotes it must be wrong because you don\u2019t agree<br /> <br /> for my part, my intent was simply to explain my own understanding. But the hostility in your responses tells me this quite simply is not welcome. I am happy to be informed otherwise on that front however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 07-15-2024, 06:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-15T08:58:49-07:00","id":1538606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1538601#post1538601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28035\" data-vbnamecard=\"28035\">Magus Maximus</a><br /> you\u2019ve written too much for me to reply to individually. But my impression is that you have essentially house rulled the majority of how the spheres function, or have played with an ST who has house rulled how the spheres function and don\u2019t actually have a solid grasp of the RAW itself. Either that or you are quite drastically missing much of what I am saying.<br /> <br /> It might be more productive to continue this in a VC style setting where ideas can be properly exchanged and I can be sure we have a chance to listen to what we intend to say rather than go off on what we believe the other to have said, as do often happens in text.<br /> <br /> but as it stands, based on how much of your complaints are either refuting things which are RAW, disliking elements which have been thr case across all editions, and how you have contradicted me as I quoted from the boom itself, especially regarding locking to a pattern, my impression is you don\u2019t have a firm understanding of the rules as written in these books. You have a firm understanding of how it works in your head, but when something in the book challenges that, rather than reevaluate your personal understanding, you just decide since it does not fit, and so makes sense to you, it simply doesn\u2019t make sense at all, therefore it cannot make sense at all.<br /> <br /> the system as written however makes a lot of sense to me. And I was hoping to provide you why it was that it did make sense, and how I come to use it. But as most of your counters amount to \u201cno, I\u2019m right and here's all the reasons you are wrong\u201d which\u2026 doesn\u2019t really leave much room for attempts to understand one another.<br /> <br /> you are of course free to have your own internal model for the game, and use that in favour of written material. But then I believe it is rather unecessary to then say everyone else who understands the system and promotes it must be wrong because you don\u2019t agree<br /> <br /> for my part, my intent was simply to explain my own understanding. But the hostility in your responses tells me this quite simply is not welcome. I am happy to be informed otherwise on that front however.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have houseruled the nonsense away, for sure. That doesn't mean I don't fully understand how RAW work. The fact that I don't like them and that they are utterly nonsensical don't take away from the fact that I understand them well enough - in fact, I understand them better than the writers themselves it would seem, since I would never implement something as convoluted as HDYDT for example.<br /> <br /> And right now you're just coping out of the matter. So you resorted to simply say &quot;oh, you don't know the rules&quot; and &quot;oh, you don't want to debate, you just want to be right&quot;. That's really some poor excuse.<br /> <br /> The reason why I object towards Forces for example, besides just how dumb it is, is also in the fact that it contradicts every other Sphere. That's my same reasoning behind the nonsense behind Correspondence. Which you're trying to evade now by using &quot;arguments&quot; that border ad hominem based on &quot;you don't understand the rules&quot;.<br /> <br /> You haven't contested why a Mage can't use Entropy 3 to bless themselves rather than Entropy 4. You haven't contested why a Mage can speed up himself using Time 2 rather than 3. And so.<br /> <br /> About the &quot;Lock on&quot; effects, we had a full length discussion about it and about its many inconsistencies of it on Ramnesis thread about the inconsistencies of the Spheres. Give me a minute and I'll link it here. And besides all the inconsistencies of it, there's also no clear reasoning behind the levels required, it's just thrown randomly, and there's also no consistency about when it is required and when it is not. So no, you haven't add anything new at all.<br /> <br /> Like you said &quot;it makes sense to me&quot;. Therefore, it is YOU who are not arguing in good faith, because you have your bias that is not open to be changed. It's not me the problem. You just seem hell bent on advocating for the holy books, irregardless of the clear inconsistencies already addressed ad nauseam.<br /> <br /> Let's be clear, I got no problem that any Sphere has any X power at any given A level. I wouldn't mind &quot;Astral Travel&quot; being Mind 1; all of those are arbitrary designs at the end of the day anyway. Although I do believe that a system of &quot;increased awesome&quot; is more elegant, it could really be whatever.<br /> <br /> But the problem is that this system, although arbitrary, needs to be internally consistent, if the goal truly is to create a functional game mechanics. And that doesn't happen AT ALL. Proof of that is that, not only do the players have doubts en masse, and it is common place to find players just throwing in Spheres and levels randomly to effects on what I always describe as &quot;gut feeling of what's right&quot; rather than a comprehensive amalgamation based on the capabilities described by each level, to the point where no 2 players can EVER agree, but you find even this infection on the part of the writers themselves - with HDYDT being just the most egregious example but hardly the only one, happening even at the core books and not as exceptions, but ALL the time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-15T09:45:26-07:00","id":1538611,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28035\" data-vbnamecard=\"28035\">Magus Maximus</a> <br /> <br /> This isn\u2019t meant to be a cop out so much as a recognition that not very much progress is being made using this format. If you truly believe I have nothing to offer you, I see no need to keep pushing you. I take no pleasure trying to discuss with those who have made up their mind.<br /> <br /> Assuming you don\u2019t mean that, however, once again, I invite you to discuss with me in real time at some point, perhaps via a chat, perhaps vc, so we can properly express ourselves.<br /> <br /> as I see it, the spheres are internally consistent, but each sphere progresses in a unique way which tells us something about the nature of that part of reality. The idiosyncarcities are actually interesting insights in to the nature of the tellurian, and I like to make use of those.<br /> <br /> My preference is to consider the implications of what I am presented with and see what sense can be made than to dismiss it as inconsistent and therefor wrong.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-15T10:58:50-07:00","id":1538616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1538611#post1538611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28035\" data-vbnamecard=\"28035\">Magus Maximus</a><br /> <br /> This isn\u2019t meant to be a cop out so much as a recognition that not very much progress is being made using this format. If you truly believe I have nothing to offer you, I see no need to keep pushing you. I take no pleasure trying to discuss with those who have made up their mind.<br /> <br /> Assuming you don\u2019t mean that, however, once again, I invite you to discuss with me in real time at some point, perhaps via a chat, perhaps vc, so we can properly express ourselves.<br /> <br /> as I see it, the spheres are internally consistent, but each sphere progresses in a unique way which tells us something about the nature of that part of reality. The idiosyncarcities are actually interesting insights in to the nature of the tellurian, and I like to make use of those.<br /> <br /> My preference is to consider the implications of what I am presented with and see what sense can be made than to dismiss it as inconsistent and therefor wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am prone to being convinced. The problem, which again, you're not truly reflecting upon, is that you are perhaps just WRONG. That's the problem. But you already have your bias that the system is just perfect the way it is, which seems than nobody agrees on.<br /> <br /> I was just doing a recap upon Ramnesis post of &quot;Sphere oddities&quot;, and I found out you advocating for absurd stuff like adding Spirit for shamanic magic, or Mind for Psychic effects. That is largely recognized by EVERYBODY as one of the most nonsensical ideas ever published for MtA, except for you.<br /> <br /> That's not a personal attack on you, just a constation that you're clearly biased and don't realize it. You may like things how they are, that's fine. But it doesn't take away from the fact that it's an utter mess. But you're letting your emotional attachment to the game and system cloud your judgement, to the point that you distort the points and arguments made in order to fit with how you feel about it. That's cognitive dissonance.<br /> <br /> It's undeniable that the system is absolutely inconsistent and incongruent throughout all of it. This is evidenced by the fact that players and storytellers are always so confused and can never agree about anything. That's not just mere happenstance. The player base aren't just a bunch of dick's wishing to shit on the material for no other reason other than being a holes. Quite the opposite, MtA has a very loyal and passionate player base that absolutely worship the game. So, the fact that LOYAL FANS are CONSTANTLY addressing their countless doubts, should be an indication that there is something wrong.<br /> <br /> I'll direct the discussion back to the Spheres oddity topic. For instance, your attempt to defend Mind + Forces for &quot;psionically controlling fire&quot; is beyond absurd, and I cannot see it as anything other than cognitive dissonance. Once again, the purpose is not to attack you, but maybe to make you realize that you're letting your emotions cloud your judgement. It's only natural to feel &quot;defensive&quot; towards something we feel emotionally attached to; I am emotionally attached to Mage to and, let's say, a D&amp;D player said &quot;yeah, Mage is garbage&quot;, that would NOT strike me on a rational level, but rather on an emotional one, and I would likewise respond emotionally, fully on cognitive dissonance, and any possibility to assess any logic reasoning behind such a statement would be gone through the window.<br /> <br /> In this example of the Mind + Forces for &quot;psionic pyrokinesis&quot; in particular, you're doing the SAME mistake as the writers in confusing game mechanics (the Spheres system) with game descriptions.<br /> <br /> The Spheres are just an abstract game mechanics. No, you DON'T need Mind AT ALL for that. In the other thread you described how you need Mind to &quot;make the fire write your name, in accordance to your own thoughts&quot;.<br /> <br /> NO. ABSOLUTELY NOT.<br /> <br /> You DON'T need Mind for that. With Forces 2 ALONE, you can use PYROKINESIS - AKA the CONTROL OF FIRE.<br /> <br /> You control Fire - or in fact, you control ANY Spells - WITH YOUR THOUGHTS ALREADY. Only Mages under Quiet create effects from subconscious emanations.<br /> <br /> Now, there's one place upon which Mind 3 + Forces 2 would be valid - but that would be to have fire being controlled by SOMEBODY'S ELSE THOUGHTS.<br /> <br /> Now, in terms of game mechanics, you DON'T need Mind in order to control fire, no matter what you want it to do. Forces 2 is what is necessary for that. That's the ABSTRACT GAME MECHANIC for it.<br /> <br /> In terms of the psychic using it, he's not describing his effect in terms of &quot;I'll Forces 2 that fire into submission!&quot;. What that psycher is doing is &quot;I'm using my psyonic Pyrokinesis to control the fire&quot;. Those are two different things.<br /> <br /> You can, of course, use Mind 3 + Forces 2 to let the fire continue bending according to your thoughts without the need to concentrate. But that's an entirely different effect.<br /> <br /> The other thing is that nobody is &quot;attacking&quot; the game, even when drawing some of the most vociferous criticisms towards it. We all love the game and wish to improve it, so it doesn't help to adopt an attitude that the game is a sacred text beyond reproach. We criticize it, viciously even, because we care, not the other way around.<br /> <br /> That being said, the game mechanics need direct, well round and well established, reasoning behind every single requirements. But what we find instead is a big series of incongruences and self contradictory information, and that's what we try to address here, so that it may be improved and corrected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 07-15-2024, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-15T11:21:32-07:00","id":1538618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1538600#post1538600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you elaborate? I have my own grivences with it being too artificial but i would like to know your opinion.<br /> <br /> As for forces i go:<br /> 1. Sight/Sense<br /> 2. Control existing minor forces (heat, sound, preasure, kinetic energy)<br /> 3. Create minor forces, control Major forces (Electromegnetism, gravity, radiation)<br /> 4. Create major forces<br /> 5. Create complex forcess efects that combine multiple forces like fire tornadoes.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I go is divide the kinds of forces between &quot;simple&quot; and &quot;complex&quot;, keeping kinetic, thermal, light and electromagnetic as &quot;simple&quot; forces, and gravity or nuclear as &quot;complex&quot; forces.<br /> <br /> I also reserve lvl 5 for &quot;Unnatural&quot; or &quot;Artificial&quot; Forces, taking example from Matter 5, creating for example a &quot;magnet&quot; that can attract non metals. I also use Forces 5 to &quot;Negate Forces&quot;, taking example from both Matter 5 and Correspondence 5. What this does is allowing you ta walk the surface of the Sun for instance, because you're completely immune to its heat or light. Or make enemies Looney Tunes drift endlessly everywhere by eliminating attrition, or creating that highly destructive little ball from the movie Men in Black that never stops bouncing because it never loses energy by colliding against obstacles, or Captain America shield and Black Panther suit. And maybe some other unforseen uses. It's basically using Forces in ways not supported by the laws of physics, all that would fall under Forces 5 (unless we're using Arch-Spheres, in which case I usually let it fall under Forces 6)<br /> <br /> Edit: after some discussion with Dataweaver however, I have decided to use Arch-Spheres to add more powah! towards Spheres rather than adding more asinine effects to them however, make lower levels more grandiose rather than trying to imagine something more complex than lvl 5 already does, thou I still reserve some to lvl 6, like the &quot;Improbability Generator&quot; that allows for things absolutely impossible to happen under Entropy 6 for example","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 07-15-2024, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-15T11:44:34-07:00","id":1538619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1538611#post1538611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[l<br /> ...as I see it, the spheres are internally consistent, but each sphere progresses in a unique way which tells us something about the nature of that part of reality. The idiosyncarcities are actually interesting insights in to the nature of the tellurian, and I like to make use of those.<br /> <br /> My preference is to consider the implications of what I am presented with and see what sense can be made than to dismiss it as inconsistent and therefor wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>And here is the entire problem, and why I'm saying that this all streams towards your own personal cognitive dissonance bias. You have assumed the position that the system is RIGHT <i>at priori</i>, and that it is YOUR job to work with it and to try to make some sense out of it because that's how it is supposed to be.<br /> <br /> But that just WRONG. Because this kind of reasoning doesn't allow for adaptability or for improvement of the system - since it is what it is, what has to change is how you adapt to it, rather than the system being adapted to what is the needs of the game.<br /> <br /> As for the &quot;idiosyncrasies&quot; of the system, again, the Spheres are ABSTRACTIONS for GAME MECHANIC PURPOSES ONLY.<br /> <br /> The Spheres are NOT some sort of hermetic philosophical take about the metaphysics of the world. Or at the very least, it shouldn't be.<br /> <br /> I've also claimed on several other occasions that I am in favor of &quot;alternative Spheres&quot; for that exact same reason, well, not only that but this is one of the reasons, because all too often players confuse Spheres with metaphysics or with the setting, and that's NOT the case AT ALL.<br /> <br /> The so called &quot;idiosyncrasies&quot; of the Spheres should only ever exist insofar as they make sense in the context of the setting and the necessary transposition of the setting's assumptions towards game mechanics.<br /> <br /> Which is why I, for example, agree that Mind 1 should allow you to increase your mental attributes, because it makes sense that changing your own mind is a relative simple task - to the point that one can do it without Magik at all (not on the same scale of course, but that's not my point, obviously Magik can accomplish more than just simple meditation or will).<br /> <br /> That however should NOT be translated to &quot;Consensus dictates that one's own Mind is made of softer clay than the rest&quot;.<br /> <br /> We as players should NOT have to do mental gymnastics and rationalize random decisions in order to understand the Spheres; they should be clear and concise irregardless of interpretation or point of view. Your example about how the &quot;Correspondence is the Sphere of Connections&quot; is a grave cautionary tale; while it may well be true, such understanding should ONLY exist within the confines of Paradigm, and the Sphere of Correspondence, as a GAME MECHANIC TOOL, should work equally well towards Mages that adhere to it as well as to Mages that view it as just plain Space Manipulation.<br /> <br /> What's more, we as players should NEVER be required to HAVE to adhere to a certain metaphysical position, whatever it is, to make use of those game mechanics. If a Sphere can only be made sense under a strict worldview, then that Sphere is BADLY WRITTEN AND SHOULD BE CHANGED.<br /> <br /> If Correspondence can only properly be understood under the metaphysical view of &quot;connections&quot;, than Correspondence is BADLY DESIGNED AND SHOULD BE CHANGED","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-15T14:02:11-07:00","id":1538622,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28035\" data-vbnamecard=\"28035\">Magus Maximus</a><br /> you have put a lot of words in my mouth here.<br /> <br /> but you have made your sentiments clear.<br /> <br /> I shall no longer expect a response to my invitation","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-15T15:59:54-07:00","id":1538632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1538622#post1538622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28035\" data-vbnamecard=\"28035\">Magus Maximus</a><br /> you have put a lot of words in my mouth here.<br /> <br /> but you have made your sentiments clear.<br /> <br /> I shall no longer expect a response to my invitation</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thank you for your kind invitation and please apologize for my... Intrusive words. I'm not a... People's person. I don't do it on purpose, I'm just terrible at being civil for whatever reason. Anyways, thanks for the invitation but I don't have discord, and I also don't have much time in my life, I'm a father of 5 kids and my newest one is just 4 months old, so my personal life is pretty consuming of both my time and energy, but I thank you anyway </div> </div> </div>I had answered, but I don't know if you saw it or if it goes to your private message or not.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, I unfortunately have to decline.<br /> <br /> And it's not my intention to &quot;put words in your mouth&quot;. I'm not trying to make it personal. I'm just pointing that we are all creatures of passion. We like to believe ourselves to be rational, but we are not. Most of the time, we will argue on emotion, not reason. And that's only natural. You have biases, I have biases, everybody has biases and that's the shadows in the cave from which we will construct our worldviews. I too will have my points based on my biases and my emotional attachments to those.<br /> <br /> My point was just to make you aware of that, so that you can see that there's other ways to look at these issues.<br /> <br /> &quot;My preference is to consider the implications of what I am presented with and see what sense can be made than to dismiss it as inconsistent and therefor wrong.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's your own personal bias. And that's fine, it is entirely within your prerogatives to have that mindset.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, I also have my own bias insofar that I want systems that are clear and concise, and if I don't have that, I would rather have it changed.<br /> <br /> That's my worldview and my bias <br /> <br /> And both are fine and work well for each of us, but it must be understood that those may not be the same worldviews for others.<br /> <br /> There are, therefore, legitimate criticisms that can be made towards the rules; if that's not how you view it, it's fine for you, but it's not an universally accepted view. That's all.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-15T17:41:52-07:00","id":1538642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1538595#post1538595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The hard part is getting enriched nuclear material. That's what's hard to get. You need some heavy industry for that, and precision equipment for the centrifuges.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually the hard part is to harvest enough material.<br /> <br /> You can locate Uranium with Matter 1. It isn't particularly rare, if not outright common. With magical location it isn't hard to find large enough amounts of it.<br /> <br /> The equipment to mine it is very specialized and controlled, but not more complex than any other mining operation.<br /> <br /> Once you have it... Enrichment is just sorting isotopes. This is Matter 3 at most, you'll be able to make higher quality than you actually need by far.<br /> <br /> From there you can make a pure Uranium bomb, or use it to make Plutonium for a more powerful artifact. If you really want to go all out, add pure Hydrogen for a fusion bomb.<br /> <br /> Matter 3 and some legwork is all you need to make an A Bomb if you really want to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T06:21:47-07:00","id":1538649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1537817-m20-correspondence-questions?p=1538642#post1538642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually the hard part is to harvest enough material.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I wasn't referring to make an A bomb using Magik, I meant doing it in rl.<br /> <br /> Getting enough uranium isn't that hard, you'll always find somebody willing to smuggle it for you.<br /> <br /> The hard part is centrifuge it in massive industrial installations without anybody finding out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T14:13:15-07:00","id":1538674,"title":"","content":"Ok, you're right on that, without magic the hard part is to enrich the stuff.<br /> <br /> By the way, acquiring large quantities is hard, but in small portions you can legally buy it online.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}